  "raw": {
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/FAU-Medicine---Galen-Building/Lead-Clinical-Medical-Assistant_REQ22894": {
      "title": "Lead Clinical Medical Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-12\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The Florida Atlantic University Medical Group is seeking a Lead Clinical Medical Assistant in Boca Raton, FL. The Lead Clinical Medical Assistant supports the Clinical Supervisor in overseeing daily   clinical operations and serves as a key resource and leader for the Medical Assistant team. This position serves as a role model in demonstrating sound judgement, maintaining professionalism, and supporting the Clinical Supervisor in maintaining a safe, efficient, and patient centered environment. This position helps ensure patient flow, consistent clinical standards, accurate   documentation, and compliance with organizational policies and procedures. P rovides day-to-day guidance, training, and support to clinical   sta ff while maintaining a strong focus on patient care and service excellence.   Key Responsibilities:   Serve as a clinical resource and point of contact for Medical Assistants and clinical   support sta ff .   Assists the Clinical Supervisor with daily coordination of clinical operations and   workflow.   Monitor patient flow and help identify and resolve operational or clinical workflow   issues.   Provide guidance, coaching, and support to Medical Assistants to promote   consistent performance and adherence to established standards.   Assist with onboarding, orientation, training, and competency assessment of new   clinical sta ff .   Support implementation and maintenance of clinical policies, procedures, and best   practices.   Help ensure exam rooms, equipment, supplies, and clinical areas are properly   maintained and prepared for patient care.   Monitor compliance with infection prevention, safety, documentation, and   regulatory requirements.   Assist with sta ff scheduling, coverage, and workflow assignments as directed by the   Clinical Supervisor.   Perform and oversee appropriate clinical duties within the scope of practice of the   Medical Assistant role.   Promote accurate and timely documentation in the electronic medical record.   Assist providers and clinical sta ff with patient care, procedures, and coordination of   services.   Identify performance, workflow, or patient-care concerns and communicate them   promptly to the Clinical Supervisor.   Participate in quality improvement initiatives, audits, and clinical process   improvement projects.   Promote a positive, professional, and collaborative work environment.   Provide exceptional patient service and model appropriate communication and   professionalism.   Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Clinical Supervisor or   leadership.   Explore Living in Palm Beach County   The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB     Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent and one year of appropriate experience required. Current Medical Assistant certification/registration required. Current BLS/CPR certification required or obtainable within the required timeframe. Excellent communication, organizational, problem-solving, and interpersonal skills required. Ability to prioritize multiple responsibilities and work effectively in a fast-paced clinical environment required. Strong knowledge of clinical workflows, patient care procedures, infection control, and medical documentation required. Completion of an accredited Medical Assistant program preferred. Minimum of 2–3 years of clinical Medical Assistant experience preferred. Previous leadership, mentoring, or lead experience preferred. Salary: $25.00 Hourly. College or Department: OPS - COM: Clinical Services Personnel Location: FAU Medicine - Galen Building Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5 p.m. Application Deadline: 2026-10-19 Special Instructions to Applicant: This recruitment has been reopened; all previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. This position may close without prior notice. Temporary positions are not established positions and are paid from OPS funds. Temporary positions are usually not eligible for benefits and retirement; however, they may be eligible for health insurance coverage depending on the average hours worked per week. They provide full-time or part-time employment in an exempt or non-exempt employment situation based on job duties and salary in accordance with the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA). Temporary positions do not have layoff rights and may be terminated without prior notice. Applicants hired into Temporary positions may apply for a regular appointment should a vacancy become available. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Title-II-Digital-Accessibility-Manual-Testing-Coordinator--Student-Accessibility-Services_REQ22975": {
      "title": "Title II Digital Accessibility Manual Testing Coordinator, Student Accessibility Services",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-12\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking a Title II Digital Accessibility Manual Testing Coordinator. - Boca Raton, FL. Summary of responsibilities: Conducts comprehensive manual accessibility testing of websites, web applications, software, mobile applications, and digital documents using established accessibility standards, including WCAG 2.1 Level AA and Section 508. Performs manual testing using keyboard-only navigation, screen readers, assistive technologies, browser accessibility features, and other appropriate testing methods to identify accessibility barriers that may not be detected through automated testing. Evaluates digital documents, including PDFs and other electronic content, for accessibility, structure, navigation, reading order, headings, alternative text, tables, forms, links, and other applicable accessibility requirements. Documents accessibility findings in clear, actionable reports that identify the location of each issue, applicable WCAG success criterion or accessibility requirement, description of the barrier, impact, and recommended technical remediation. Tracks accessibility issues through resolution and maintains documentation of testing results, remediation activities, and outstanding barriers. Collaborates with OIT, Public Service, OCR9, SAS, the College for Online Learning and Continuing Education, and other university stakeholders to support consistent implementation of digital accessibility requirements. Provides training and technical assistance on Section 508, WCAG 2.1 Level AA, manual accessibility testing, accessible document creation, and faculty and staff responsibilities for developing accessible digital content. Serves on the Title II Accessibility Committee and contributes to the development, review, and implementation of accessibility policies, procedures, and practices. Performs other job-related duties as assigned. FAU Benefits and Perks   If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers: Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more.   State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans.   State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program.   Sick Leave Pool Program.   Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion).   Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day   Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply).     For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php     Explore Living in Palm Beach County   The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB   Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization; or a bachelor's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization and two years of appropriate experience required. Salary: $51,000. annually. Exempt Administrative, Managerial, Professional (AMP) College or Department: Division of Student Affairs Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8am - 5pm. Some weekends and nights are required. Application Deadline: 2026-10-16 Special Instructions to Applicant: APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Associate-General-Counsel_REQ23012": {
      "title": "Associate General Counsel",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-12\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking an Associate General Counsel. - Boca Raton, FL. Responsible to the General Counsel. Provides primary in-house counsel on a broad array of external transactional arrangements, including contract and lease negotiation, drafting, and compliance. May be delegated responsibility for the overall direction and management of specific areas of the legal function of the Board of Trustees or the university. Assists as directed by the General Counsel in planning, organizing, and directing all legal activities involving the Board of Trustees or the university. Advises and consults with university or Board officials on legal rights and obligations and assists in the formulation of legal policy. Summary of Responsibilities: Responsible for managing university litigation and administrative law matters, including coordinating with the State’s Division of Risk Management on the selection and assignment of outside counsel, overseeing discovery, trial preparation, mediation, and settlement negotiations.   Provides legal advice to the Division of Student Affairs on a variety of issues related to student discipline, crisis response, academics, financial matters, residency, contracts, international programs, Title IX, the Americans with Disabilities Act, free speech, and religious accommodations.  Supervises the University’s processes for subpoena responses and document production and advises institutional clients on compliance with Florida’s public records laws and Federal privacy laws.  Serves as a liaison to the University Police Department, the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX, Public Affairs, and the University’s Risk Manager. Appears and attends at court and mediation as necessary. Performs other job-related duties as required or deemed appropriate. FAU Benefits and Perks   If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers:   Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more.   State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans.   State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program.   Sick Leave Pool Program.   Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion).   Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day   Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply).     For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php     Explore Living in Palm Beach County   The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: Juris doctor degree from an accredited institution and two years of appropriate experience is required. Salary: $165,000.00 - $185,000.00 USD Annually. Administrative Managerial Professional (AMP) College or Department: Office of University General Counsel Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8:00am - 5:00pm Application Deadline: 2026-10-26 Special Instructions to Applicant: APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
