    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Deputy-Athletic-Director_REQ22996": {
      "title": "Deputy Athletic Director",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-12\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking a Deputy Athletic Director - Boca Raton, FL. The Deputy Athletic Director reports to the Vice President of Intercollegiate Athletics and provides executive leadership and operational oversight for the entire department. Responsible for supporting and leading department-wide operations, strategy, and acting on behalf of the Vice President when assigned. Summary of Responsibilities Acts on behalf of the Vice President/Director of Athletics. Supports and provides administrative and operational leadership across all athletic units, ensuring alignment and continuity. Translate strategic priorities into operational plans, timelines, and measurable objectives. Supports and leads internal strategy, overseeing the Chief Financial Officer and related internal units, serving as a key advisor to the executive leadership team. Oversee the business and day-to-day operations of the athletic department. Lead cross-functional initiatives that affect the broader athletics department. Oversee and supervise internal departments that include Sports Medicine, Strength and Conditioning, Facilities and Events, Compliance, Mental Health and Performance, and Student Athlete Success Center departments, amongst others. Provides sport oversight for Men’s Soccer, coordinating resources and program support. Reviews, approves, and recommends financial decisions for assigned areas; collaborates closely with the Athletics CFO on budget planning and resource allocation. Represents the department professionally in university, conference, community, and corporate settings. Participates as a member of the athletics executive leadership team. Performs other job-related duties as assigned. FAU Benefits and Perks If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers: Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more. State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans. State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program. Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php Explore Living in Palm Beach County The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization and six years of appropriate experience; or a bachelor's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization and eight years of appropriate experience required. Salary: $205,000 annually. Exempt Administrative, Managerial, Professional (AMP) College or Department: University Athletics Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8am - 5pm. Weekends and nights as needed. Application Deadline: 2026-10-19 Special Instructions to Applicant: APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Contract-Administrator_REQ22176": {
      "title": "Contract Administrator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-12\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking a Contract Administrator in Boca Raton, FL. The Contract Administrator plays a critical role in supporting the Office of Sponsored Programs (OSP). Responsible for drafting, reviewing, negotiating, and administering a wide range of sponsored research agreements. Ensures compliance with federal, state, sponsor, and institutional requirements, while fostering effective communication and strong working relationships with faculty, staff, sponsors, and collaborators. Summary of Responsibilities: Review, draft, redline, and negotiate externally funded research agreements, amendments, and non-financial agreements such as NDAs and MOUs from federal, state, foundation, and local government agencies. Works with FAU General Counsel and coordinates with other internal offices such as Export Control, IT, Research Integrity, Technology Development to address intellectual property, indemnification, publication rights, data use, confidentiality, and regulatory compliance (Institutional Review Board (IRB), Institutional Animal Care and Use Committee (IACUC), Institutional Biosafety Committee (IBC), etc.). Obtain required legal approvals for contractual documents and facilitate their execution in accordance with delegated signature authority. Serve as backup for the issuance of outgoing subaward and the complete subaward process. Serve as a resource to OSP staff and stakeholders on complex contracting issues and interpretation of contractual terms. Contribute to the continuous improvement of internal contract and subaward processes in alignment with university policies and compliance standards. Maintain accurate records, logs, documentation, and electronic files related to contracts and outgoing subawards. Stay current on evolving federal and state regulations, sponsor requirements, and institutional policies. Attend relevant regional meetings, trainings, and professional development activities as appropriate. Performs other job-related duties as assigned. FAU Benefits and Perks   If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers:  Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more. State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans. State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program. Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php Explore Living in Palm Beach County The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization; or a bachelor's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization and two years of appropriate experience required. Strong organizational and communication skills, with the ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously required. Strong written and verbal communication skills required. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills required. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, and external partners required. Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines required. Knowledge of federal, state, and sponsor regulations, including Uniform Guidance required. Demonstrates experience in contract management, contract drafting, negotiation, and compliance required. Preferred experience in contract negotiation, research administration, or grants management. Salary: $65,000 - $72,000 annually. College or Department: Division of Research: Sponsored Programs Contract Administration Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Application Deadline: 2026-10-26 Special Instructions to Applicant: This recruitment has been reopened; all previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. This position may close without prior notice. This is a research or research-related support position. As required by Florida Statutes Section 1010.35, a Foreign Influence Screening may be required. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Laboratory-Assistant_REQ22973": {
      "title": "Laboratory Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-09\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The Department of Psychology at Florida Atlantic University is seeking a highly motivated part-time Laboratory Assistant in Boca Raton, FL. The research for Dr. Pehlivanoglu's lab investigates resilience and vulnerability in cognitive, affective, and social functioning across adulthood and aging by employing a multimethod approach that integrates behavioral experiments/surveys with physiological (e.g., eye-tracking) and neuroimaging (EEG/ERP, and fMRI) measures. The Laboratory Assistant will play a central role in establishing a new laboratory from the ground up while receiving extensive mentorship in research design, cognitive neuroscience methods, EEG and fMRI data acquisition and analysis, statistical analysis, and scientific writing. The position also offers extensive training in cognitive and affective aging research within a collaborative and supportive research environment. The Laboratory Assistant will also have opportunities to contribute to scientific publications and conference presentations. This is a part-time, 1-year position with the possibility of renewal for a second year based on performance. This position is ideal for an individual interested in pursuing training in neuroscience, psychology, biomedical engineering, computer science, cognitive science, or a related field after gaining intensive research experience. The Laboratory Assistant will work closely with the principal investigator on all aspects of research, including: Assisting with the establishment of laboratory infrastructure and research workflows. Setting up, maintaining, and troubleshooting EEG or other research equipment. Developing and optimizing EEG preprocessing and analysis pipelines. Assisting with fMRI preprocessing and analysis pipelines. Programming behavioral experiments (e.g., PsychoPy, PsychoJS, E-Prime, MATLAB). Participating in study design, project development, and interpretation of research findings. Managing research databases and ensuring high-quality data organization. Assisting with participant recruitment, scheduling, and testing. Supervising and training undergraduate research assistants. Assisting with statistical analyses, data visualization, and reproducible research workflows. Contributing to manuscript preparation, conference presentations, and grant-related activities. Performing general laboratory management and administrative tasks as needed. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. Explore Living in Palm Beach County   Florida Atlantic University has six different campuses. The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB   Minimum Qualifications: A high school diploma or equivalent from an accredited institution is required. Salary: $18.00 USD - $23.00 USD hourly Non-Exempt Other Personnel Service (OPS) College or Department: College of Science Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, part-time up to 29 hours. Application Deadline: 2026-10-23 Special Instructions to Applicant: Temporary positions are not established positions and are paid from OPS funds. Temporary positions are usually not eligible for benefits and retirement; however, they may be eligible for health insurance coverage depending on the average hours worked per week. They provide full-time or part-time employment in an exempt or non-exempt employment situation based on job duties and salary in accordance with the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA). Temporary positions do not have layoff rights and may be terminated without prior notice. Applicants hired into Temporary positions may apply for a regular appointment should a vacancy become available. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Chair-and-Professor_REQ22774-1": {
      "title": "Chair and Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-09\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking a Chair and Professor- Boca Raton, FL The College of Education (COE) at Florida Atlantic University is accepting applications for department chair of Curriculum and Instruction ( https://www.fau.edu/education/academicdepartments/curriculum-instruction/ ). The department chair serves as senior faculty member and administrator of the academic department. At the departmental level, this person is responsible for faculty recruitment and development; instructional program development and quality enhancement; coordination of departmental research and service programs; evaluation of personnel; and, through the dean, representing the department within and beyond the university. The chair also maintains relationships with students, other administrators, university councils and committees, alumni, professional organizations, and various other public and private groups. In conjunction with the COE dean, the chair develops the department's annual budget request, manages the course schedule of the department’s 15+ undergraduate and graduate programs, administers expenditures of the allocated funds, works closely with department program coordinators and program committees, evaluates faculty and staff, and manages other resources available to the department. The chair facilitates effective relationships within and across department programs and, as a member of the COE's leadership team, works collaboratively with the dean and other unit leaders to guide the work of the COE. The COE at Florida Atlantic University is committed to providing an accessible and supportive environment that promotes academic excellence and prepares all students for success in a broad range of educational and professional contexts. Candidates who can contribute to that goal are encouraged to apply and to identify their strengths in this area. Minimum Qualifications: Doctoral Degree in Curriculum and Instruction or related area from an accredited institution; hold rank of full professor at the time of appointment required. Preferred Qualifications: • Leadership in preservice and in-service teacher education or related areas. • Administrative, managerial, and financial knowledge and skills to effectively lead an academic department. • Success as a collaborative leader, with effective communication and interpersonal skills in an environment that encourages engagement with varied perspectives and experiences. • Record of teaching/ research/ service demonstrating commitment to public education. • Experience and success working in constructive partnerships with large school districts. Salary: Commensurate with Experience College or Department: Department of Curriculum and Instruction Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: N/A Application Deadline: 2026-11-16 Special Instructions to Applicant: This recruitment has been reopened; all previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: FAU’s Career Page permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. PLEASE NOTE: A maximum of five (5) documents may be attached to your application. If more than five (5) documents are required for submission, please combine additional documents into a single attachment to not exceed the maximum permitted. The site permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. Candidates wishing full consideration are to provide the following: a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and three professional letters of recommendation. In the event that individuals writing letters of recommendation wish to remain confidential, please email letters to the search committee chair, Dr. Elizabeth Sacks (evillare@fau.edu). Transcripts: The selected candidate for this position is required to submit an official transcript sent directly from the institution for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Similarly, for degrees from outside the United States, the evaluation by an organization belonging to the National Association of Credential Evaluation (NACES), with an indication of the documents the evaluation was prepared from (official transcripts, diplomas, dissertation abstracts) is required for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Transcripts must be issued to Florida Atlantic University, not to the individual applicant. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/OPS-Physician_REQ22903": {
      "title": "OPS Physician",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-08\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking multiple Physicians in the Department of Student Health Services. - Boca Raton, FL. Student Health Services at Florida Atlantic University invites applicants for a temporary part-time Physician. Florida Atlantic University (FAU) Student Health Services is located in beautiful Boca Raton with additional smaller campuses in Jupiter and Davie. FAU is an exciting and dynamic school that is rapidly growing. At FAU SHS, we seek to provide high quality, culturally competent care in a manner that is respectful, fiscally responsible, and developmentally appropriate. We combine a wide range of medical, counseling, preventative, and wellness services to help students remain healthy and succeed academically.  Summary of Responsibilities Include:  Obtains appropriate medical history and performs accurate physical examination.  Comforts with acute medical care, primary care, and chronic disease management.  Experience with basic primary care procedures such as laceration repairs and pap smears.  Orders and correctly interprets appropriate diagnostic studies to assist with management.  Develops an appropriate assessment and treatment plan consistent with findings and utilizes medication and other treatment modalities appropriately.  Provides education and information on the diagnosis and treatment plan including appropriate preventive and health enhancement strategies and actions.  Refers for additional consultation, evaluation, and treatment when clinically indicated.  Practices within the scope of privileges and licensure.  Uses evidence-based strategies to guide diagnosis and treatment.  Adheres to policies and established workflows for delivery of patient care.  Boca Raton – Main Campus OPS physicians will serve as the Provider of the Day and will: Serve as the primary clinical resource for nurses, NPs, and PAs, providing guidance and support for clinical questions. Provide clinical support and coverage for day-to-day OPS operations. Jupiter – Satellite Campus OPS physicians will provide support for: OPS provider inbox coverage, including addressing clinical questions and follow-up needs. Inventory support, including assisting with inventory-related needs and coordination. FAU Benefits and Perks   If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers:  Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more.  State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans.  State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program.  Sick Leave Pool Program.  Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion).  Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day   Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply).    For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php     Explore Living in Palm Beach County  The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB   Minimum Qualifications: Doctor of Medicine (MD) or Doctor of Osteopathic Medicine (DO) degree from an accredited institution or college of osteopathic medicine required. Unrestricted MD or DO License to practice in state of Florida by date of hire. Board certification in internal medicine, medicine-pediatrics, or family practice. DEA registration. Current BLS certification. Experience using electronic health records. Demonstrated ability to provide culturally competent care for diverse population. Strong interpersonal, verbal and written communication skills. Highly effective problem solving and decisions making skills. The provider must be willing to travel between the Main Campus in Boca Raton and the satellite campus in Jupiter, as needed. Salary: $115 hourly. Other Personnel Services (OPS) College or Department: Division of Student Affairs: Student Health Services Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8am - 5pm. Application Deadline: 2026-10-22 Special Instructions to Applicant: This recruitment has been reopened; all previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. This position may close without prior notice. Temporary positions are not established positions and are paid from OPS funds. Temporary positions are usually not eligible for benefits and retirement; however, they may be eligible for health insurance coverage depending on the average hours worked per week. They provide full-time or part-time employment in an exempt or non-exempt employment situation based on job duties and salary in accordance with the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA). Temporary positions do not have layoff rights and may be terminated without prior notice. Applicants hired into Temporary positions may apply for a regular appointment should a vacancy become available. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Operations-Assistant_REQ22991": {
      "title": "Operations Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-06\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The College of Business at Florida Atlantic University is seeking an Operations Assistant in Boca Raton, FL. The Operations Assistant supports the daily operations of the Boca Schmidt Family Complex and Executive Education programs by providing facility, event, and customer service support to students, faculty, staff, and visitors. This position works closely with the Building Manager to help maintain a safe, professional, and welcoming environment while coordinating operational activities, facility needs, and program logistics in a fast-paced setting. Essential Duties: Support the daily operations of the Boca Schmidt Family Complex, serving as a resource for students, faculty, staff, and guests. Assist with Executive Education programs and events, including orientations, graduations, evening classes, and other special activities; coordinate event setup, breakdown, catering, and logistics. Conduct routine facility inspections to ensure classrooms, offices, common areas, and entrances are clean, secure, and operating effectively; report and follow up on maintenance and safety concerns. Assist the Building Manager with facility maintenance, repairs, security coordination, inventory management, purchase orders, and vendor or contractor communications. Manage incoming deliveries, maintain operational records and documentation, and support administrative functions related to building operations. Provide excellent customer service by addressing inquiries, troubleshooting facility-related issues, and ensuring concerns are communicated through the appropriate channels. Primarily support operations on the Boca Raton campus, with occasional travel to and support of Executive Education activities and facilities on the Davie and Fort Lauderdale campuses. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. Explore Living in Palm Beach County   The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent from an accredited institution or higher required. A high level of professionalism and dependability is required. Be personable while at the same time maintaining a high level of professionalism. Demonstrate excellent customer service and interpersonal skills. Excellent verbal and written skills; Requires flexibility, willingness to work side by side with students, and the ability to work in a high-demand, high-pace environment. Possess leadership and teamwork skills to effectively work with department and University personnel to achieve the goals of the department. Salary: $19.16 to $21.55 per hour. College or Department: COB: Executive Degree Programs Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday – Friday, 8:00 AM -5:00 PM. Some nights and weekends as needed. Application Deadline: 2026-10-20 Special Instructions to Applicant: Temporary positions are not established positions and are paid from OPS funds. Temporary positions are usually not eligible for benefits and retirement; however, they may be eligible for health insurance coverage depending on the average hours worked per week. They provide full-time or part-time employment in an exempt or non-exempt employment situation based on job duties and salary in accordance with the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA). Temporary positions do not have layoff rights and may be terminated without prior notice. Applicants hired into Temporary positions may apply for a regular appointment should a vacancy become available. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Enrollment-Processing-Coordinator_REQ22567": {
      "title": "Enrollment Processing Coordinator (Updated)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-06\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The Department of Undergraduate Admissions at Florida Atlantic University is seeking an Enrollment Processing Coordinator in Boca Raton, FL. The position analyzes data, conducts special projects, collaborates with students, faculty, staff, and external stakeholders, and may participate in recruitment initiatives and student outreach efforts. Summary of Responsibilities: Review and input data from domestic and international transcripts into the Student Information System using Optical Character Reading software and/or data entry. Review and input SAT/ACT/AP/AICE/IB data. Ensure data accuracy and integrity to support internal operations and external reporting requirements. Match documents or test scores to the correct students' files. Export and upload student records to the university’s document management system (e.g., OnBase). Draft and maintain professional email correspondence for timely and effective communication with applicants, university departments, and external partners, including the Registrar’s Office, University Advising, and Parchment. Resolve complex student inquiries and cross-department issues that require troubleshooting. Identify trends and provide actionable recommendations for process improvements. Assist with testing applications or other new technology. Participate in regular training on Slate CRM, Optical Character Recognition software,  Document Imaging, and LinkedIn Learning for professional and skill development. Participate in a handful of recruitment events, front lobby operations, phone coverage, and prospective student inquiries as needed to ensure a positive applicant experience. Perform other job-related responsibilities as assigned by the Director or Associate Director. FAU Benefits and Perks   If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers:  Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more.  State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans.  State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program.  Sick Leave Pool Program.  Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion).  Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day   Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply).    For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php     Explore Living in Palm Beach County   The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: A bachelor's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization and two years of appropriate experience; or a master's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization required. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Strong analytic and interpretation skills. The ability to stay focused in a fast-paced environment, critically think and troubleshoot, as well as attention to detail are critical in this position. The ability to craft professional email communication to follow up with applicants and co-workers is essential. Salary: $49,631.76 annually. Administrative, Managerial, Professional (AMP) College or Department: Undergraduate Admissions Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8am - 5pm. Occasional evenings and weekends are required. Application Deadline: 2026-10-13 Special Instructions to Applicant: This recruitment has been reopened; all previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. This position may close without prior notice. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Maintenance-Specialist_REQ21740": {
      "title": "Maintenance Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-06\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking a Maintenance Specialist. - Boca Raton, FL. The Maintenance Specialist plays a vital role in the comprehensive oversight, coordination, and execution of maintenance and operational activities within residential life facilities. This role ensures that all corrective, preventive, and emergency work requests are properly assessed, assigned, and completed while maintaining high standards of safety, functionality, and service. Summary of responsibilities: Independently oversee, inventory, direct, control, review and assign all corrective preventive emergency work requests, day to day repairs, maintenance work and activities of maintenance and utility matters in the resident life facilities. Consult with the Assistant Director, Housing Facilities on a weekly basis concerning repairs. (Repairs can include but may not be all inclusive of minor repairs and/or replacement of plumbing repairs such as fixtures, valves, flushometers, traps; electrical repairs to fixtures or devices, defective bulbs, switches, fuses and receptacles in buildings; HVAC work and repairs such as regulate steam or hot water equipment, thermostats; assist with other HVAC, carpentry, painting and other building related mechanical and structural devices). Evaluate independently the need for repairs for any and all defects, deterioration, and wear and tear on the facilities. Schedule repair work and coordinate work with Assistant Director, Housing Facilities . Routinely inspect all residential facilities and assure that deficiencies are corrected. Enter, receive and report all work orders through the Housing on-line Work Order System (School Dude). Review and assign, in consultation with the Assistant Director, Housing Facilities , all corrective, preventive, and emergency work requests. Identify, assess damages to proper parties, and make reports when necessary on all acts of vandalism to and in the resident halls. On a daily basis, communicate with key administrative and staff personnel on special events and functions that may require special arrangements and other duties that may be required. Coordinate projects with the necessary Campus entitles to ensure a smooth transition and implementation and serve as a liaison between Housing and Campus Facilities Staff. Contact vendors and contractors and coordinate the work with the Assistant Director, Housing Facilities . Create and plan for special projects and summer renovations as needed. Develop materials and supply budget and submit for approval to Assistant Director of Housing. Participate in P-Card program and keep track of all expenditures. Communicate with the Assistant Director, Housing Facilities , Hall Coordinator, Senior Custodian, and Program Assistant regarding performance and special needs. In the absence of Assistant Director, Housing Facilities , assume the duties and responsibilities of the day to day physical plant operations and report to the Director of Housing. Assist with the assignment of student and/or temporary maintenance assistants as needed to ensure the work is being done properly and that workers have the necessary tools and supplies to complete the job. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. FAU Benefits and Perks   If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its   perks ! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers:   Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more.   State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans.   State employees   Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF)   program.   Sick Leave Pool Program.   Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at   President’s   discretion).   Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day   Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition   assistance   after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply).     For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at   https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php     Explore Living in Palm Beach County   The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the   area   a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here:   Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB   Minimum Qualifications: A high school diploma and five years of appropriate experience; or completion of an approved apprenticeship program for multiple trades and one year of appropriate experience required. Appropriate vocational/technical training may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. Salary: $23 hourly. Non-Exempt Support Personnel (SP) College or Department: Division of Student Affairs Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8am - 5pm. Some nights and weekends are required. Application Deadline: 2026-10-20 Special Instructions to Applicant: This recruitment has been reopened; all previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. This position may close without prior notice. VETERANS’ PREFERENCE: Applicants may claim Veterans’ Preference on their application. The applicant claiming preference is responsible for providing required documentation at the time of making an application in Workday for a vacant position, or prior to the closing date of the vacancy announcement. If an applicant qualifies for Veterans' Preference and the SP position, they are shown preference by the guarantee of an interview. Veterans’ Preference does not guarantee a job. For additional information, please visit https://www.fau.edu/jobs/resources/veterans/. For assistance, please contact Recruitment Services at empl@fau.edu. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Media-Relations-Assistant-Director-of-Academic-Life-and-University-Programming_REQ22613": {
      "title": "Media Relations Assistant Director of Academic Life and University Programming  ***Updated***",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-05\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking a Media Relations Assistant Director of Academic Life and University Programming - Boca Raton, FL. The Assistant Director of Media Relations for Academic Life and University Programming will develop and implement public relations strategies that advance Florida Atlantic University’s strategic priorities, elevate the University’s reputation, and strengthen visibility for academic life, student experiences, and university programming. Summary of Responsibilities: Work closely with departments, colleges, faculty, staff, and leadership across the University to promote academic and student-centered experiences, arts and culture offerings, personal enrichment programming, distinguished speakers, community-facing events, and other initiatives that position Florida Atlantic as a leading public research university and a dynamic destination for learning, discovery, and engagement. Identify, develop, write, and distribute compelling press releases, media advisories, feature stories, media pitches, society-style releases, event recaps, and related communications materials. Build and maintain relationships with local, regional, community, lifestyle, business, higher education, and specialty media outlets across Florida Atlantic’s service region. Prepare and submit society-style photo releases from designated donor, alumni, presidential, and university events to appropriate publications and society sections. Support communications and public relations strategies that advance the University’s strategic plan, strengthen brand awareness, and elevate institutional reputation. Coordinate interviews between media outlets and faculty, students, staff, leadership, and external partners. Staff media at events, announcements, press conferences, and other designated university activities. Support major university announcements and media events in coordination with the central media relations team. Help manage media relations content on FAU.edu and oversee the @FAUNews X account. Provide analytics and reporting for web news releases, media coverage, and social media activity related to the media relations function. Monitor media coverage, gather and archive news clips, and assist with reporting on media relations outcomes. Support internal communications and social media content in collaboration with other communications and marketing staff. Assist with updates to crisis communications materials and support crisis communications efforts as needed. Serve as a writer for various University news topics, leadership communications, and institutional channels as assigned. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. FAU Benefits and Perks   If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers:  Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more.  State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans.  State employees  Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF)  program.  Sick Leave Pool Program.  Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion).  Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day   Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply).  For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php   Explore Living in Palm Beach County   The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: ***Updated*** A master’s degree from an accredited institution and two years of relevant experience; or a bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution and three years of relevant experience required. Relevant experience must be in media relations. Valid Florida Driver's License required. Salary: $60,000 - $72,000 Annual. College or Department: DUC: Media Relations Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. This is an in-person position and is not eligible for remote working arrangements. Application Deadline: 2026-10-19 Special Instructions to Applicant: This recruitment has been reopened; all previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. This position may close without prior notice. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/John-D-MacArthur-Campus---Jupiter/Assistant-Director-of-Residential-Education_REQ22559": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Residential Education",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-05\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The Department of Housing and Residential Education at Florida Atlantic University is seeking an Assistant Director of Residential Education in Jupiter, FL The Assistant Director of Residential Education serves as a member of the Residential Education leadership team within the Department of Housing and Residential Education. This live-in position provides direct supervision of a Community Coordinator and a Housing Administration Coordinator, and indirect leadership to Resident Assistants and Front Desk Staff, while overseeing the residential experience across three residence halls at the Wilkes Honors College on the Jupiter Campus. The Assistant Director provides leadership for a residential experience that fosters inclusive communities and supports student learning, engagement, wellbeing, academic success, and personal development. Oversees the implementation of the department's residential curriculum, supports student conduct and critical-incident response efforts, collaborates with campus partners, and contributes to a comprehensive housing program that prioritizes student satisfaction, retention, learning, and engagement. Participates in the department's second-level on-call rotation. Staff Supervision and Leadership: Directly supervise a Community Coordinator and Housing Administration Coordinator. Provide indirect leadership and support to Resident Assistants and Front Desk Staff. Provide ongoing coaching, mentoring, supervision, performance feedback, and professional development for direct and indirect reports. Support the recruitment, selection, onboarding, training, evaluation, and development of professional and student staff. Foster a culture of learning, accountability, collaboration, student-centered decision-making, and continuous improvement. Conduct performance evaluations, establish clear expectations, and promote professional growth and accountability. Program Implementation and Assessment: Lead the implementation of the department's residential curriculum within the assigned residential area. Contribute to a comprehensive assessment plan encompassing satisfaction, retention, and student learning outcomes. Utilize data and assessment tools to enhance the residential experience. Prepare semester and annual reports that evaluate area performance and identify opportunities for continuous improvement. Collaborate with campus partners to develop and implement initiatives that support student recruitment, success, retention, and engagement.   Incident Response and Risk Management: Review on-call and incident reports to ensure timely follow-up, consistency, and appropriate response. Provide leadership and decision-making during critical incidents and emergency situations. Ensure Community Coordinators are trained in university protocols related to behavioral intervention, mental health, emergency response, facilities concerns, and student support. Participate in the departmental on-call rotation and provide after-hours leadership and consultation. Coordinate post-incident follow-up, student support, referrals, and case management while supporting Community Coordinators in addressing roommate conflicts, community concerns, and student wellbeing. Provide students with guidance, support, referrals, and developmental coaching directly and through the supervision of staff. Promote a safe residential environment through proactive risk management, policy education, and community accountability.   Student Conduct: Serve as a student conduct administrator by adjudicating alleged violations of university and housing policies. Utilize the student conduct process as an educational opportunity that promotes accountability and student development. Provide guidance and accountability to Community Coordinators regarding conduct documentation and case management. Interpret and communicate university and housing policies consistently and fairly.   Administrative and Operational Oversight: Oversee the assigned residential area to ensure operational consistency, accountability, and alignment with departmental priorities. Lead residence hall opening, closing, and semester transition processes in collaboration with Residential Education Operations and campus partners. Oversee administrative functions including occupancy management, damage billing, health and safety inspections, student records, and related processes. Monitor area budgets and utilize departmental resources responsibly. Conduct regular facility walkthroughs in partnership with Housing Facilities to identify operational needs and support timely resolution. Recommend improvements to departmental policies, procedures, and operational practices that enhance the residential student experience.   Campus Engagement: Provide operational and programmatic support for university-wide events, including Orientation, Family Weekend, Admissions initiatives, athletic events, and campus traditions. Serve on departmental committees and represent Residential Education on divisional or university committees as assigned. Develop collaborative partnerships that strengthen the residential student experience. Performs other job-related duties as assigned. FAU Benefits and Perks   If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers:  Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more.  State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans.  State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program.  Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day   Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). ​ For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php   Explore Living in Palm Beach County   The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: A master's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization and two years of appropriate experience; or a bachelor's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization and four years of appropriate experience required. Salary: $61,000 - $63,000 annually. Exempt Administrative, Managerial, Professional (AMP) College or Department: Division of Student Affairs: Housing & Residential Location: John D. MacArthur Campus - Jupiter Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8am - 5pm. Must be able to work nights and weekend as needed. Application Deadline: 2026-11-05 Special Instructions to Applicant: This recruitment has been reopened; all previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. This position may close without prior notice. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
