    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Coordinator-I--Student-Financial-Aid_REQ22957": {
      "title": "Coordinator I, Student Financial Aid",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-30\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking a Coordinator I, Student Financial Aid . - Boca Raton, FL. The Coordinator I, Student Financial Aid position supports the Office of Student Financial Aid’s mission of offering a comprehensive financial aid program that attempts to meet the financial needs of all University students. Summary of Responsibilities Analyses and evaluates financial aid information of assigned student population and determines eligibility for financial aid awards to students. Processes revisions, professional judgments, and appeals for assigned students according to the alpha division. Assists with front desk staffing during peak time, or as needed. Reviews and processes weekly financial aid reports, such as negative need and over-budget reports. Performs an initial review in OnBase of student verification documents, determines additional documents required, and requests the necessary forms and documents. Reviews tax forms and other submitted documents and makes changes in compliance with federal regulations and university policies. Advises students and families at the front desk, via phones, and Ivy Chat, regarding the processing of their financial aid application, assists with completion of forms, eligibility requirements, and documentation necessary to comply with federal, State and institutional regulations as well as policies and procedures. Assists with outbound campaign calls. Assists with FAFSA filing workshops. Assists with the Financial Wellness Program, including outreach and presentations to students. Assists with processing Florida Atlantic Cares applications. Provides ongoing support and guidance to Helios Program recipients as they navigate their academic journey and work toward degree completion. Collaborates closely with the First-Generation Student Success Office to provide support, resources, and guidance to students who indicate a need for assistance. Works with the Dean of Students staff to administer the Gerstner Grant and all other need-based aid programs for students. Works with the Dean of Students staff to identify and assist Homeless/Foster Youth and Homeless students for aid and Federal Work-study opportunities. Serves on committees and working groups with the Dean of Students office to provide programming and assistance as part of their Care-Based model of student support. Collaborates with campus partners to support outreach, intervention, and other initiatives designed to promote student persistence, retention, and graduation. Performs other job-related duties as assigned. FAU Benefits and Perks If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers: Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more. State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans. State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program. Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php Explore Living in Palm Beach County The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in an appropriate area of specialization; or a bachelor's degree in an appropriate area of specialization and two years of appropriate experience required. Salary: $62,000 - $64,272 Annually. Exempt Administrative, Managerial, Professional (AMP) College or Department: Student Financial Aid: Student Success Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Occasional weeknights and weekends required. Application Deadline: 2026-10-14 Special Instructions to Applicant: APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/American-Sign-Language-Interpreter_REQ22831": {
      "title": "American Sign Language Interpreter",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-29\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The College of Medicine at Florida Atlantic University is seeking an American Sign Language Interpreter in Boca Raton, FL. The OPS Part-Time ASL Interpreter provides American Sign Language (ASL) interpretation services to support a deaf faculty member within the College of Medicine. The interpreter will facilitate effective communication during meetings, presentations, conferences, research activities, trainings, and other university-related events. Summary of Responsibilities: Provide accurate and professional ASL interpretation services for faculty meetings, presentations, seminars, and departmental events. Interpret communications involving medical education, healthcare, scientific research, and academic discussions. Facilitate communication between the faculty member and colleagues, students, researchers, healthcare professionals, and external collaborators. Review meeting materials and presentation content in advance when available to ensure familiarity with technical terminology and subject matter. Maintain strict confidentiality regarding research activities, patient-related information, and university business in accordance with applicable privacy and confidentiality requirements. Collaborate with faculty and departmental staff to coordinate interpretation needs and scheduling. Attend in-person and virtual meetings as needed. Adhere to the professional standards and code of ethics established by the Registry of Interpreters for the Deaf (RID). Other job-related duties as assigned. Explore Living in Palm Beach County   Florida Atlantic University has six different campuses. The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB   Minimum Qualifications: A high school diploma or equivalent is required. Fluency in American Sign Language (ASL) and English required. RID Certification (NIC or CI/CT), or equivalent professional credentials required. Experience providing ASL interpretation services in higher education, healthcare, medical, scientific, or research settings required. Strong knowledge of professional interpreting practices and ethics required. Excellent interpersonal, communication, and organizational skills required. Ability to accurately interpret complex medical and scientific terminology required. Ability to work collaboratively with all levels of faculty, staff, and students. Exceptional verbal and written communication skills are essential for success in this position required. Exceptional customer service, organizational and time management skills required. Experience in a higher education institution, medical school, or hospital highly preferred. Salary: $55.00 Hourly. College or Department: OPS - COM: Population Health Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Part time up to 15 hours weekly Monday - Friday. Application Deadline: 2026-10-13 Special Instructions to Applicant: Temporary positions are not established positions and are paid from OPS funds. Temporary positions are usually not eligible for benefits and retirement; however, they may be eligible for health insurance coverage depending on the average hours worked per week. They provide full-time or part-time employment in an exempt or non-exempt employment situation based on job duties and salary in accordance with the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA). Temporary positions do not have layoff rights and may be terminated without prior notice. Applicants hired into Temporary positions may apply for a regular appointment should a vacancy become available. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check."
