    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Coordinator--Student-Accessibility-Services_REQ21751": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Student Accessibility Services",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking a Coordinator for Student Accessibility Services. - Boca Raton, FL. The Coordinator of the Student Accessibility Services (SAS) reports to the SAS Associate Director and is responsible for ascertaining and providing for the special needs of FAU students with disabilities, particularly students with medical, psychological, physical, learning, hearing, and visual disabilities. This includes assessing needs in the academic setting, reviewing disability documentation (DSM-5 and ICD Codes), counseling students regarding disability-related issues and academics, and ensuring the provision of approved accommodations. Summary of responsibilities: Maintain a caseload of students. Review and interpret disability documentation. Meet with students and utilize an interactive process to determine and grant academic, housing, and ESA accommodations. Work with students to assist with academic concerns, professor/course-related issues, accountability, and organization. Maintain case notes for each student interaction. Prepare and provide presentations to students, faculty, and staff regarding disability issues, laws, and awareness. Take part in weekly Coordinator case review meetings and monthly staff meetings. Act as Student Accessibility Services liaison or representative on Student Affairs and FAU committees. Performs assigned special projects and job-related duties as needed. FAU Benefits and Perks   If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its   perks ! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers:   Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more.   State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans.   State employees   Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF)   program.   Sick Leave Pool Program.   Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at   President’s   discretion).   Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day   Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition   assistance   after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply).     For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at   https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php     Explore Living in Palm Beach County   The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the   area   a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here:   Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB   Minimum Qualifications: A master's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization; or a bachelor's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization and two years of appropriate experience required. Salary: $48,000 - $51,000 annually. Exempt Administrative, Managerial, Professional (AMP) College or Department: Division of Student Affairs Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8am - 5pm. Some nights and weekends are required. Application Deadline: 2026-10-12 Special Instructions to Applicant: This recruitment has been reopened; all previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. This position may close without prior notice. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Clinical---Off-Campus-Location-COM-use-only/Acute-Care-Surgeon--Emergency-General-Surgery---Surgical-Critical-Care----Assistant-Professor-Associate-Professor-Full-Professor_REQ22950": {
      "title": "Acute Care Surgeon (Emergency General Surgery & Surgical Critical Care) - Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/Full Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The Department of Surgery at Florida Atlantic University (FAU) seeks a full-time academic surgeon who is board certified/eligible in General Surgery and Surgical Critical Care. The primary responsibility of this position is to serve as a Surgical Critical Care physician, providing comprehensive management of critically ill surgical patients in the intensive care unit. The faculty member will also participate in General Surgery call and have a significant role in the education, supervision, and mentorship of FAU General Surgery residents.   The faculty member will report directly to the Chair of the Department of Surgery and work collaboratively with the General Surgery Residency Program Director and Department leadership.   Responsibilities Serve primarily as a Surgical Critical Care/ICU attending, providing approximately 14–16 daytime ICU shifts per month, generally 12-hour shifts. Direct daily multidisciplinary ICU rounds and management of critically ill postoperative and surgical patients. Manage complex critical care conditions including respiratory failure, mechanical ventilation, sepsis and septic shock, hemodynamic instability, multiorgan failure, acute kidney injury, nutritional and metabolic disorders, and complex postoperative complications. Perform appropriate critical care procedures within clinical privileges, including airway management, central venous and arterial catheter placement, and other bedside procedures. Provide critical care consultation and coordinate care with surgical and multidisciplinary teams. Participate in ICU quality improvement, patient safety, and morbidity and mortality activities. Participate in approximately 4–5 General Surgery call assignments per month, including evaluation and management of acute surgical conditions, inpatient consultation, operative care, and perioperative management. This is not a trauma surgery position; trauma surgery will not be a primary clinical responsibility. Provide direct supervision and bedside teaching of General Surgery residents in the ICU and during General Surgery call. Participate in resident evaluations, curriculum development, didactic conferences, M&M conferences, journal clubs, case conferences, and other educational activities. Maintain an educational environment consistent with ACGME and FAU standards. The successful candidate will receive an academic faculty appointment in the Florida Atlantic University Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine, Department of Surgery, with academic rank commensurate with qualifications and experience. Minimum Qualifications: • MD or DO degree from an accredited medical school. • Completion of an ACGME-accredited General Surgery residency. • Board certification/eligibility in General Surgery. • Fellowship training and board certification/eligibility in Surgical Critical Care. • Eligibility for an unrestricted Florida medical license and appropriate clinical privileges. • Demonstrated commitment to academic medicine, graduate medical education, teaching, and resident mentorship. Salary: Commensurate with qualifications and experience. College or Department: Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine Location: Clinical - Off Campus Location (COM use only) Work Days and Hours: N/A Application Deadline: 2026-12-31 Special Instructions to Applicant: This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: FAU’s Career Page permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. PLEASE NOTE: A maximum of five (5) documents may be attached to your application. If more than five (5) documents are required for submission, please combine additional documents into a single attachment to not exceed the maximum permitted. The site permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. Candidates wishing full consideration are to provide the following: a cover letter and curriculum vitae. Transcripts: The selected candidate for this position is required to submit an official transcript sent directly from the institution for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Similarly, for degrees from outside the United States, the evaluation by an organization belonging to the National Association of Credential Evaluation (NACES), with an indication of the documents the evaluation was prepared from (official transcripts, diplomas, dissertation abstracts) is required for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Transcripts must be issued to Florida Atlantic University, not to the individual applicant. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Clinical---Off-Campus-Location-COM-use-only/Associate-Program-Director--General-Surgery--Assistant-Professor-Associate-Professor-Full-Professor-_REQ22949": {
      "title": "Associate Program Director, General Surgery (Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/Full Professor)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The Florida Atlantic University Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine, Department of Surgery, is seeking a highly qualified, academically accomplished, and motivated Associate Program Director (APD) for the General Surgery Residency Program. The APD will serve as a senior member of the residency leadership team and will work closely with the Chair, Program Director, faculty, residents, and institutional leadership to support the continued development and excellence of the program. The APD will assist in the educational, clinical, administrative, and operational leadership of the residency program, including curriculum development, resident education and evaluation, clinical and operative experience, scheduling and rotation management, recruitment, faculty engagement, scholarly activity, quality improvement, patient safety, resident wellness, and ACGME/ABS compliance.    The APD will participate actively in resident conferences, M&M, Clinical Competency Committee activities, recruitment, mentorship, and continuous program improvement, with a particular emphasis on developing technically proficient, academically engaged, ethical, accountable, and independent surgeons.   The APD will report to the Chair of the Department of Surgery and General Surgery Residency Program Director and will function as a key leadership partner in advancing the mission and strategic goals of the FAU Department of Surgery and General Surgery Residency Program. The APD will provide leadership in resident education, faculty development, clinical operations, resident assessment, recruitment, scholarly activity, quality improvement, and program development while maintaining strong and collaborative relationships with residents, faculty, service chiefs, hospital leadership, affiliated clinical sites, and the FAU Office of Graduate Medical Education. The APD will be expected to identify opportunities for improvement, develop and implement innovative educational initiatives, promote accountability and professionalism, support resident and faculty development, and contribute meaningfully to the continued growth and success of the residency program.   The successful candidate will be an ABS board-certified surgeon with a demonstrated commitment to graduate medical education, surgical education, patient safety, quality improvement, and resident professional development. Prior experience in GME leadership, ACGME accreditation, resident evaluation, recruitment, simulation, or quality improvement is preferred.   The position will include protected administrative time appropriate to the scope and responsibilities of the role and will be evaluated annually based on educational outcomes, resident development, operative experience, recruitment and retention, scholarly activity, faculty engagement, patient safety, quality improvement, accreditation performance, leadership, and contribution to the continued advancement of the program. The successful candidate will receive an academic faculty appointment in the Florida Atlantic University Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine, Department of Surgery, with academic rank commensurate with qualifications and experience. Minimum Qualifications: • MD or DO degree from an accredited medical school. • Completion of an ACGME-accredited General Surgery residency. • Board certification/eligibility in General Surgery. • Eligibility for an unrestricted Florida medical license and appropriate clinical privileges. • Demonstrated commitment to academic medicine, graduate medical education, teaching, and resident mentorship. Salary: Commensurate with Experience College or Department: Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine Location: Clinical - Off Campus Location (COM use only) Work Days and Hours: N/A Application Deadline: 2026-12-31 Special Instructions to Applicant: This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: FAU’s Career Page permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. PLEASE NOTE: A maximum of five (5) documents may be attached to your application. If more than five (5) documents are required for submission, please combine additional documents into a single attachment to not exceed the maximum permitted. The site permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. Candidates wishing full consideration are to provide the following: a cover letter and curriculum vitae. Transcripts: The selected candidate for this position is required to submit an official transcript sent directly from the institution for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Similarly, for degrees from outside the United States, the evaluation by an organization belonging to the National Association of Credential Evaluation (NACES), with an indication of the documents the evaluation was prepared from (official transcripts, diplomas, dissertation abstracts) is required for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Transcripts must be issued to Florida Atlantic University, not to the individual applicant. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Harbor-Branch-HBOI/Executive-Director-of-Harbor-Branch-Oceanographic-Institute_REQ22917": {
      "title": "Executive Director of Harbor Branch Oceanographic Institute",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking an Executive Director of Harbor Branch Oceanographic Institute- Ft Pierce, FL. The Executive Director of the Harbor Branch Oceanographic Institute (HBOI) provides visionary leadership to advance the Institute as a world-class center for oceanographic research, innovation, and impact. Reporting to the Vice President for Research, this position drives scientific excellence, industry engagement, strategic partnerships, and resource development while strengthening HBOI's national and international reputation. The Executive Director leads the growth of HBOI's research enterprise, expands external funding opportunities, cultivates relationships with government, industry, philanthropic, and academic partners, and fosters interdisciplinary collaboration across Florida Atlantic University. The role oversees the Institute's research, operational, administrative, and financial functions, including stewardship of HBOI's unique waterfront campus and specialized facilities, while creating opportunities for faculty, staff, and students to contribute to solving critical coastal, ocean, and environmental challenges. As HBOI's chief ambassador, the Executive Director champions innovation, entrepreneurship, workforce development, and transformative research that advances ocean discovery, environmental sustainability, and economic development. Summary of Responsibilities: Provide the vision and leadership necessary to advance HBOI as a world-class oceanographic research and innovation institute. Advance and strengthen HBOI’s core environmental, coast, and ocean research enterprise, supporting scientific excellence and growth in areas such as marine ecosystem conservation, coastal and ocean health, water quality, aquaculture and food security, marine biotechnology, ocean exploration, coastal defenses, and related fields. Serve as the primary external ambassador for HBOI, developing strong relationships with industry executives, government leaders, federal agencies, donors, research organizations, and other strategic partners. Develop and execute a comprehensive strategy for industry engagement and collaboration, including attracting companies to conduct research, testing, and technology development at HBOI. Work with university leadership to establish a consistent framework for industry partnerships that ensures appropriate returns to FAU through sponsored research, student experiences, faculty collaboration, infrastructure investment, and other institutional benefits. Significantly increase sponsored research and diversify HBOI’s funding portfolio, with particular emphasis on federal, defense, industry, and other external research support. Identify and cultivate opportunities for large-scale multidisciplinary and multi-institutional research programs and partnerships. Build interdisciplinary research initiatives that connect environmental and marine science with ocean engineering, autonomous systems, artificial intelligence, biotechnology, and other emerging technologies to address complex coastal and ocean challenges. Expand connections with the defense, maritime, autonomous systems, ocean technology, biotechnology, and related industries where HBOI and FAU have distinctive capabilities. Create meaningful pathways for students to engage with industry through internships, research experiences, sponsored projects, workforce development, and employment opportunities. Work collaboratively with faculty at HBOI and throughout Florida Atlantic to strengthen interdisciplinary research and identify opportunities to connect faculty expertise with industry and government needs. Develop relationships with federal and state agencies and strengthen HBOI’s visibility and competitiveness for major research initiatives and funding opportunities. Work closely with the Harbor Branch Oceanographic Institute Foundation and its Board of Directors to align Foundation activities with the strategic needs and opportunities of HBOI and to expand external engagement. Partner with Florida Atlantic’s advancement team to identify and cultivate philanthropic support for HBOI priorities. Lead a diverse and effective team and provide oversight of the Institute’s research, administrative, operational, and budgetary functions. Provide strategic oversight and stewardship of HBOI’s complex 144-acre waterfront campus and 32 facilities, including specialized laboratories, engineering and testing spaces, aquaculture systems, small-boat and waterfront operations, educational and public-facing facilities, housing and critical infrastructure, ensuring safe and efficient operations and long-term alignment with the Institute’s research, education, and outreach missions. Recruit, develop, and retain outstanding faculty and staff and foster a collaborative environment that supports excellence, innovation, and entrepreneurship. Work collaboratively with the HBOI Faculty Assembly and other university stakeholders in the shared governance of the Institute. Serve on the Vice President for Research’s leadership team and contribute to the broader growth and direction of Florida Atlantic’s research enterprise. Represent HBOI and Florida Atlantic at national and international conferences, meetings, industry gatherings, and scientific and governmental forums. FAU Benefits and Perks If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers: Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more. State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans. State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program. Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in an appropriate area of specialization and seven years of appropriate experience; or a bachelor's degree in an appropriate area of specialization and nine years of appropriate experience required. Preferred Qualifications: Candidates must possess a doctoral degree in oceanography, marine science, engineering, biology, biotechnology, chemistry, aquaculture or another field relevant to the mission of Harbor Branch. Candidates should have significant senior-level leadership and management experience in a research-intensive university, research institute, government laboratory, industry research organization or comparable environment. Candidates must have or be able to obtain a Personnel Security Clearance (PCL). Strong candidates will demonstrate: • A distinguished record of scientific, engineering or research accomplishment and the professional stature necessary to lead a major research institute. • A sustained record of securing and managing significant public and/or private research funding. • Demonstrated experience developing substantive partnerships with industry, including sponsored research, technology development, testing, commercialization, joint initiatives or other collaborative programs. • A track record of cultivating relationships with senior executives, government leaders, federal agencies and other external partners. • Experience leading large, multidisciplinary research initiatives and building effective teams across organizational boundaries. • Demonstrated success growing research programs, developing new revenue sources and translating institutional assets and expertise into strategic partnerships. • Strong communication, interpersonal and relationship-building skills and the executive presence necessary to serve as the public face and leading advocate for HBOI. • Experience related to environmental and coastal science, marine ecosystem conservation, ocean technology, maritime systems, national defense, autonomous systems, marine science, biotechnology or other areas aligned with Florida Atlantic’s strategic research priorities is strongly preferred. Salary: Salary Commensurate with Experience Exempt Administrative, Managerial, Professional (AMP) College or Department: Division of Research Location: Harbor Branch (HBOI) Work Days and Hours: Monday-Friday some weekends Application Deadline: 2026-11-07 Special Instructions to Applicant: APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Assistant-Director--Online-Student-Experience---Pathways_REQ22906": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Online Student Experience & Pathways",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The Center for Online and Continuing Education (COCE) at Florida Atlantic University is seeking an Assistant Director, Online Student Experience & Pathways in Boca Raton, FL. The Assistant Director for Online Student Experience & Pathways develops and cultivates new enrollment pathways for online programs, with particular emphasis on expanding Florida Atlantic's reach to out-of-state, traditional-age undergraduate students, including first-time-in-college and transfer populations. Central to the role is developing an intentional online student experience that extends beyond virtual instruction. Under the concept of \"Learning Online in Paradise,\" the Assistant Director will help create opportunities for online students to build meaningful connections with Florida Atlantic, including its campuses, traditions, student organizations, events, services, and university community. Whether students engage with Florida Atlantic on campus or remain in their home communities, the Assistant Director will develop intentional opportunities that foster a sense of belonging, university identity, peer connections, and participation in the broader Florida Atlantic experience. Enrollment Pipeline & Market Development Identify geographic markets, institutions, student populations, and academic interests that present opportunities for sustainable online enrollment growth. Develop and implement strategies to establish new enrollment pipelines for Florida Atlantic's online undergraduate programs, with particular emphasis on out-of-state FTIC and transfer students. Develop scalable recruitment models and partnership strategies that move prospective students from awareness and interest through application and enrollment. Collaborate with university admissions and marketing partners to develop targeted communication and recruitment strategies for identified markets. Online Student Experience \"Learning Online in Paradise\" Lead the development of \"Learning Online in Paradise\" as an intentional experience, creating opportunities for online students to experience the benefits of Florida Atlantic's location, campuses, traditions, resources, and university community while maintaining the flexibility of online learning. Design engagement opportunities that connect online students with the physical campus through orientation experiences, campus visits, signature events, athletics, student organizations, career programming, commencement activities, and other university experiences. Partner with Student Affairs, academic colleges, Career Services, campus recreation, athletics, student organizations, and other university stakeholders to expand participation opportunities for online students. Out-of-State Student Engagement & Belonging Develop engagement strategies that foster connection, belonging, and university identity among out-of-state online students who remain in their home state throughout their academic program. Create virtual and regional engagement opportunities that connect online students with one another, Florida Atlantic faculty and staff, alumni, and the broader university community (i.e., regional student meet-ups and community-building events, athletic events, and connect with alumni in their areas). Pathway & Student Journey Design Map the prospective and enrolled student journey for targeted online populations and identify opportunities to strengthen conversion, onboarding, engagement, and persistence. Develop and document workflows that coordinate student movement across recruitment, application, admission, onboarding, enrollment, and student success processes. Collaborate with university partners to clarify roles, responsibilities, handoffs, communication timelines, and escalation processes. Create playbooks, process maps, communication plans, and other operational resources supporting pathway implementation. Data, Systems & Enrollment Analytics Monitor pipeline performance and adjust strategies based on application, conversion, enrollment, and persistence outcomes. Utilize student information systems, CRM platforms, enrollment dashboards, and other university technologies to monitor student pipelines and engagement. Produce regular reports and presentations summarizing trends, engagement activity, outcomes, and opportunities for improvement. Establish performance metrics for new pathway initiatives and evaluate return on recruitment and engagement efforts. Perform other job-related duties as assigned FAU Benefits and Perks   If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers:  Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more.  State retirement options, including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans.  State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program.  Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day   Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). ​ For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php   Explore Living in Palm Beach County   The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization and two years of appropriate experience; or a bachelor's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization and four years of appropriate experience required. Master's degree in appropriate area and three years of relevant experience preferred. Salary: $75,000 - $80,000 annually. College or Department: COCE: Online Student Support Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday – Friday, 8:00 AM -5:00 PM. Some nights and weekends as needed. Application Deadline: 2026-10-12 Special Instructions to Applicant: APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Coordinator-of-Accounting-and-Finance_REQ22670": {
      "title": "Coordinator of Accounting and Finance",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-28\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking a Coordinator of Accounting and Finance . - Boca Raton, FL. The Coordinator of Accounting and Finance enhances the academic effectiveness of Florida Atlantic University and its students, faculty and staff by providing support services specifically related to fiscal management, personnel services, purchasing, bursar functions and administrative technology. Summary of Responsibilities: Conducts the preliminary review of expense justification requests, purchase requisitions, and payment requests for completeness and necessity of purchase. This entails an evaluation of account codes, budget balances, and available cash. Ensures that all contracts are completed prior to payment requests or requisitions moving forward by submitting all contracts for review and signature to the Division’s Director of Finance and Accounting. Ensures P-Card posting occurs within university-established timelines. Maintains expense control spreadsheets for the department indexes and ensures that all expense logs are maintained by staff and reconciled in a timely manner. Performs secondary reconciliation of expenses. Reviews all encumbrances to ensure accuracy. Provides monthly updates of expenses to the Director and reports any concerns to the Associate Director of Finance and Accounting. Benchmarks current revenue and expenses to previous years. Assists in maintaining accurate balances of all departmental open/blanket purchase orders and analyzes invoices for accuracy. Provides review of all Internal Agreements, invoices & JEs prior to the Director and client signatures, as necessary. Enters Requisitions into Workday and ensures that POs are created and invoices are approved and paid in a timely manner. Assist other departments in the division with their purchasing as needed.  Enters journals into Workday to recognize revenue from credit card payments and other departments, and enters other journals as needed. Creates monthly revenue reconciliations between the accounting system and billing system and makes correcting entries as needed.    Enters purchase requests into Owl Central to obtain prior approval and confirm budget availability.  Creates and/or reviews on a timely basis Daily Tender Summaries, Credit Card Reconciliations, and Payroll Reconciliations and researches and resolves discrepancies with members of the Campus Recreation team and obtains approval on completed items from the Campus Recreation Director and Assistant Director of Finance and Accounting. Provides monthly updates on revenue collection, noting which invoices are past 15 days due.  Participates in meetings of the Campus Recreation leadership team. Communicates changes in University finance policy to departmental staff. Assists with Audit Compliance of all Campus Recreation financial and administrative procedures.  Evaluates and provides feedback/recommendations regarding all departmental financial procedures. Responsible for processing payments, entering requisitions, and P-card purchases related to club sports. Provides assistance to the Assistant Director of Sports Programs Assists professional staff with spending authorizations and expenditures related to conference and candidate recruitment travel. Serves as the backup HR partner to help process student employees' onboarding and offboarding. Staff Development and Supervision: Oversees the hiring, training, scheduling, and supervision of Finance Intern(s). Provides support and insight for student staff development opportunities. Assists with the development of departmental strategic plan and annual assessment materials. Serves on committees and provides assistance to the department and division as needed.  Perform other job-related duties as assigned. FAU Benefits and Perks   If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers:  Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more.  State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans.  State employees  Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF)  program.  Sick Leave Pool Program.  Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break   (at President’s discretion).  Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day   Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty -   Tuition assistance after   6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply).  For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at  https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php   Explore Living in Palm Beach County   The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here:  Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB   Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in an appropriate area of specialization, or a bachelor's degree in an appropriate area of specialization and two years of appropriate experience required. Salary: $48,000 - $51,500 annually. Exempt Administrative, Managerial, Professional (AMP) College or Department: Division of Student Affairs: Finance Operations Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8a.m. - 5p.m. Some nights and weekends required. Application Deadline: 2026-10-12 Special Instructions to Applicant: This recruitment has been reopened; all previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. This position may close without prior notice. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Community-Coordinator_REQ22910": {
      "title": "Community Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking a Community Coordinator in Boca Raton, FL. The Community Coordinator supports students' success by fostering an inclusive and welcoming community where students feel a sense of belonging. This role helps develop and implement programs, initiatives, and engagement opportunities that promote student wellbeing, strengthen connections, and enhance the overall student experience. Summary of Responsibilities:   Interview, select, train, supervise, and evaluate a team of 8-14 Resident Assistants. Assist with implementing and assessing a residential curriculum. Contribute to a comprehensive assessment plan and utilize data to make evidence-based enhancements to programs and services. Actively recruit, advise, develop, and support the Community Council. Manage hall budgets for programming and supplies. Fiscally responsible for the use of a university purchasing card.  Assist with hall opening/closing procedures.  Advise students with personal and emotional conflicts and act as a referral agent for other campus resources. Provide follow-up and support student wellbeing. Administer Student Conduct process through adjudication of cases involving policy violations.  Interpret and ensure compliance with departmental and university policies, guidelines, and other relevant regulations. Educate staff and students to enforce policies. Serve as a customer service representative of the department and university. Maintain positive working relationships with custodians, maintenance specialists, and other facilities personnel.  Execute health and safety inspections for the residence hall. Review on-call reports and incident reports daily and provide necessary follow-up. FAU Benefits and Perks   If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers:  Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more.  State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans.  State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program.  Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day   Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). ​ For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php   Explore Living in Palm Beach County   The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in an appropriate area of specialization; or a bachelor's degree in an appropriate area of specialization and two years of appropriate experience required. Salary: $51,500.00 - $53,045.00 Annually. Administrative Managerial Professional (AMP). College or Department: Student Affairs. Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8:00 am - 5:00 pm. Some evenings and weekends. Application Deadline: 2026-10-22 Special Instructions to Applicant: APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Assistant-Vice-President--Strategic-Philanthropy_REQ22938": {
      "title": "Assistant Vice President, Strategic Philanthropy",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University seeks a deeply experienced, creative, and dynamic fundraiser to help lead a relationship-focused, results-oriented, donor-centered advancement team.   Florida Atlantic University, established in 1961, officially opened its doors in 1964 as Florida's fifth public university. Today, the University serves more than 30,000 undergraduate and graduate students across six campuses located along the southeast Florida coast and is ranked as a top public university by U.S. News and World Report.   FAU is an energetic and fast-growing institution, determined to propel itself to the forefront of innovation and scholarship. In recent years, the University has doubled its research expenditures and outpaced its peers in student achievement rates. Our students are bold, ambitious, and ready to take on the world.   Reporting directly to the Vice President of Institutional Advancement and CEO of the FAU Foundation and serving as a key member of the senior leadership team, the AVP of Strategic Philanthropy will lead the organization’s individual giving strategy while securing, stewarding, and growing major philanthropic investments that advance the mission of Florida Atlantic University’s Colleges and units.   In close partnership and collaboration with the Vice President for Institutional Advancement, and the Assistant Vice President for Schools and Units, the school/college deans, and additional university leadership, the AVP will establish ambitious fundraising goals and develop performance metrics for development units and staff; driving efficiency and maximizing philanthropic support; utilize data analytics tools to identify trends and formulate strategies to drive the Advancement Officer metrics framework; work with Advancement Officer and campus partners to create and execute donor strategies; provide training and mentorship to fundraising staff; and maintain their own portfolio of high-level prospects. The AVP of Strategic Philanthropy works closely with Regionally assigned Directors of Advancement and will assist in developing and executing comprehensive strategies to identify, cultivate, solicit, and steward major gift donors, leadership donors, planned giving prospects, and campaign contributors. This position manages a portfolio of high-capacity donors and prospects while building a sustainable pipeline of philanthropic support to achieve annual and long-term fundraising goals.   The Assistant Vice President of Strategic Philanthropy is a valued member of the senior leadership team and will guide, coach, and supervise a team of Directors of Advancement focused on regional priorities, Legacy Giving, Foundation Relations, and Scholarships, and Student Affairs. This position will ensure the team meets philanthropic goals and works with committee members, volunteers, and community stakeholders to strengthen relationships and inspire transformational investments that support FAU’s mission. The successful candidate will experience a commitment to Advancement at the very top from the President; a seasoned, dynamic Vice President of Institutional Advancement with a winning track record; innovative and committed Provost and Deans; and the opportunities and responsibilities appropriate for fundraising leaders to complete Florida Atlantic’s next campaign.   Summary of Responsibilities: Provide strong leadership and guidance to a team of professionals, fostering a high-performance culture, including directly supervising a staff of 7, which includes: Regional Directors of Advancement (4) and an Assistant Scholarships & Student Affairs Director of Advancement Legacy Giving Executive Director and Associate Director Foundation Relations Executive Director and Assistant Director Set clear performance metrics, ensuring alignment with overall fundraising objectives, and conduct regular performance reviews. Strategically partner with the Vice President for Institutional Advancement and the Assistant Vice President for Schools and Units in all areas of fundraising, as well as preparing for a future campaign. Play a critical role in the development and execution of the University’s overall fundraising strategy, including partnering with the Vice President and other University leaders in setting goals, establishing strategies and plans, and assessing performance. Work collaboratively with the Assistant Vice President for Schools and Units, all Colleges, university leadership, units and programs, and advancement staff to creatively address and provide opportunities for donor-focused solicitations addressing donors’ holistic interests across the entirety of FAU; Serve as a collaborative peer and strategic thought partner to finance leadership regarding grants, contracts, budgets, and the formation of essential policies and procedures.   Successful Candidate Will Have the Following Characteristics: A leadership-level talent capable of overseeing and improving strategic regional major gift efforts, working effectively with ambitious teams, and contributing to a successful advancement and alumni relations operation. Collaborative, goal-oriented, strategic, and highly motivated working style. The ability to demonstrate leadership, take initiative, problem-solve, act independently and as a member of a team, successfully collaborate, handle multiple tasks simultaneously, and prioritize. The ability to demonstrate strategic thinking, good judgment, maturity, and personal integrity. Excellent interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills, and an ability to communicate and collaborate effectively with a diverse campus community including senior administrators, faculty, staff, and students, as well as donors, prospects, alumni, and community leaders. Ability to use tact and diplomacy to handle a broad range of high-level and sensitive situations with diverse personalities, and the ability to adeptly respond to challenges. Able to work beyond traditional work hours and on occasional holidays. Ability to travel as needed and adjust working hours to meet requirements of special tasks and events. Ability to translate academia-speak to diverse audiences. ​ FAU Benefits and Perks If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers: Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more. State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans. State employees  Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF)  program. Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php   Explore Living in Palm Beach County The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: A master's degree and at least 10 years of fundraising experience; A successful fundraising track record and strength in developing thoughtful and creative donor strategies in a complex organization; A deep knowledge and understanding of philanthropy and fundraising; Strong leadership skills and exceptional analytical and problem-solving skills; Demonstrable strength in developing thoughtful donor strategies, preferably in higher education; Progressive experience supervising and managing staff, budgets, and developing and implementing annual goals; Extensive experience managing and working with high-level donors with demonstrated measurable success; Experience in fundraising and capital campaigns; and Familiarity with fundraising software and analytical tools, as well as excellent verbal and written communication skills; Ability to successfully engage and motivate diverse groups of individuals at all levels, including staff, alumni, and volunteers; Familiarity with performance metrics and accountability measures and how to apply them to motivate and empower staff and educate stakeholders about the essentials of fundraising; Experience in strategic planning and a commitment to, and understanding of, the building steps for taking a research university’s advancement program to a new level of success; Ability to build trusting and productive relationships with the University’s leaders, colleagues, volunteers, donors, faculty, and staff; Demonstrated ability to develop cultivation and successful solicitation strategies across all university priorities, and the ability to acquire and creatively address donors’ interests and needs; Knowledge of university personnel policies and procedures is desirable; and Developing and implementing special events. Proficiency in using standard computer applications, including word-processing, spreadsheet, CRM software, calendaring, email, and online applications, and a working knowledge of social media. Raiser's Edge experience is helpful. Salary: $250,000 - $260,000. Annually Administrative, Managerial and Professional (AMP) FLSA Exempt College or Department: Division of Institutional Advancement Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday – Friday. This position will require travel and/or work outside of standard business days and hours related to donor activities and engagement. Application Deadline: 2026-10-17 Special Instructions to Applicant: **This recruitment may close without prior notice ** APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Westgate/Licensed-Clinical-Social-Worker_REQ22883": {
      "title": "Licensed Clinical Social Worker",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking a Licensed Clinical Social Worker - Westgate, FL. The Licensed Clinical Social Worker (LCSW) provides therapy, crisis intervention, and case management while creating treatment plans based on patient assessments. The LCSW works with healthcare teams to deliver integrated care, ensure compliance with regulations, and maintain accurate records. Summary of Responsibilities Provide individual, family, and group psychotherapy to patients of all ages. Conduct biosocial assessments and develop individualized treatment plans. Provide individual psychotherapy sessions on a weekly or biweekly basis. Develop and modify treatment plans based on clinical progress and changing patient’s needs. Educate patients and families on mental health conditions and coping strategies. Use evidence-based therapeutic modalities such as CBT and DBT, motivational interviewing and trauma informed care. Works with substance use and addiction populations on an outpatient basis, serving substance use/dependency, active additions, court-ordered to attend local outpatient drug programs for individual and group therapy for those who have been arrested or are in current legal issues for DUIs, trafficking, DWI's or child custody cases related. Collaborate with medical providers, case managers, and other team members to support integrated care. Offer crisis intervention and risk assessments, including safety planning when necessary. Design and implement behavioral health programs aligned with the FQHC's mission, while monitoring outcomes and recommending enhancements based on patient and community needs. Assist patients in navigating social service systems, including housing, food security, and benefits access. Maintain timely, accurate, and confidential documentation in the electronic health record (EHR). Maintains patient scheduling level at 32 hours per week with average of 28 patients seen and 8 hours allocated for administrative time to assure note closure to be completed. Ensure compliance with all relevant federal, state, and local regulations, including HIPAA. Stay updated on trends, best practices, and behavioral health regulations to guide program improvements. Participate in audits, quality assurance reviews, care management meetings, and team discussions to uphold service standards. Support outreach to neighborhood schools/communities as directed. Participate in regular staff meetings, staff training programs, supervisory sessions, and accept the responsibility for aiding the development of positive team relationships as requested. Adhere to agency policy, procedures, and the professional code of ethics. Uphold ethical standards and best practices in line with NASW Code of Ethics and HIPAA regulations. Perform other ad hoc and job-related duties and projects as assigned. FAU Benefits and Perks If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers: Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more. State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans. State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program. Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php Explore Living in Palm Beach County The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in an appropriate area of specialization; or a bachelor's degree in an appropriate area of specialization and two years of appropriate experience required. Salary: $65,000.00 - $80,000.00 Annually. Administrative Managerial Professional (AMP). College or Department: College of Nursing. Location: Westgate Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8:30 am - 5:00 pm. Application Deadline: 2026-10-05 Special Instructions to Applicant: APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Director-of-Donor-Relations-and-Stewardship_REQ22927": {
      "title": "Director of Donor Relations and Stewardship",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-17\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University seeks a creative and motivated Advancement professional to fill a critical role on a relationship-focused, results-oriented, donor-centered advancement team. The Director of Donor Relations and Stewardship role requires a creative, thoughtful fundraising professional to design a comprehensive, meaningful acknowledgment and stewardship program for major and leadership gifts across the university. This role’s core responsibilities are to develop and execute an annual calendar of strategic donor relations deliverables, communications, and engagement opportunities (including a future Campaign) that show appreciation for support and inspire donors to give at higher levels. Summary of Responsibilities: Design and implement a comprehensive donor relations program, including; Define optimal donor journeys at established giving levels Create tools to facilitate meaningful and personalized donor experiences, including impact and stewardship reports, digital assets, etc. Implement a robust acknowledgment and stewardship program Develop targeted recognition opportunities for established donor levels Develop the voice for Florida Atlantic donor messaging, providing regular communication to the advancement team about University-wide milestones and happenings and ensuring the team receives updated presentation materials and email content Work collaboratively and effectively with Foundation leadership and advancement team members to create and implement individualized stewardship plans for major prospects; serve as a trusted advisor across the university programs to develop, manage and execute stewardship programs for donors Help train and educate Advancement and University staff on industry best practices in donor relations; work closely with staff across the University to instill and reinforce a culture of philanthropy Work collaboratively with the advancement communications team to develop corresponding materials; ensure all donor-facing materials align with overarching University communications and that materials complement and elevate donor stewardship Coordinate with the Director of Events and the Office of the President to ensure Foundation-wide event strategy aligns with the donor stewardship and communications calendars Expand and manage the acknowledgment process, ensuring gifts are thanked by the appropriate individual(s) in a timely manner and recorded in the database Continuously assess and adjust stewardship strategy as necessary to exceed donor expectations Manage and develop an effective team, providing effective communication, leadership by example, guidance and resources to staff; evaluate staff performance regularly and ensure staff team is appropriately and effectively supported Regularly report department performance, needs, and opportunities to the Assistant Vice President of Advancement Operations with quarterly updates to the AVP Schools and Units, AVP Strategic Philanthropy, and as needed, the VP of Institutional Advancement. Get creative, design stewardship and communications strategies that excite and engage our community across Colleges and programs! Successful Candidate Will Have the Following Characteristics: Collaborative, goal-oriented, strategic, and highly motivated working style. The ability to demonstrate leadership, take initiative, problem-solve, act independently and as a member of a team, successfully collaborate, handle multiple tasks simultaneously, and prioritize. The ability to demonstrate strategic thinking, good judgment, maturity, and personal integrity. Excellent interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills, and ability to craft compelling language to demonstrate program value and impact and to communicate and collaborate effectively with a diverse campus community including senior administrators, faculty, staff, and students, as well as donors, prospects, alumni, and community leaders. Ability to use tact and diplomacy to handle a broad range of high-level and sensitive situations with diverse personalities, and the ability to adeptly respond to challenges. Able to work beyond traditional work hours and on occasional holidays. Ability to travel as needed and adjust working hours to meet requirements of special tasks and events. Ability to translate academia-speak to diverse audiences.   FAU Benefits and Perks If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers: Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more. State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans. State employees  Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF)  program. Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php   Explore Living in Palm Beach County The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree with a minimum of 7 years of experience in development, stewardship, events, and/or communications; experience directly supporting donor relations preferred. Ability to implement fundraising best practices while adapting for the uniqueness of the donor or program; experience in complex, multi-faceted organizations preferred. Regarded as a trusted expert internally in the field of donor relations and stewardship. Demonstrated success in managing a team towards achieving organizational goals. Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously and prioritize responsibilities effectively. Collaborative team-player willing to work across departments to achieve the best possible results. Proficiency in using standard computer applications, including word-processing, spreadsheet, CRM software, calendaring, email, and online applications, and a working knowledge of social media. Raiser's Edge experience is helpful. Salary: $100,000 - $120,000. Annually Administrative, Managerial and Professional (AMP) FLSA Exempt College or Department: Division of Institutional Advancement Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday – Friday. This position will require travel and/or work outside of standard business days and hours related to donor activities and engagement. Application Deadline: 2026-10-17 Special Instructions to Applicant: **This recruitment may close without prior notice ** APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Director-of-Advancement--College-of-Business_REQ22926": {
      "title": "Director of Advancement, College of Business",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-17\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University seeks an experienced fundraising leader to join a relationship-focused, results-oriented, donor-centered advancement team. Opened in 1964, Florida Atlantic University serves more than 30,000 students across six beautiful campuses in South Florida. Among FAU’s 10 colleges is the College of Business, home to over 9,000 students, diverse academic departments, and an impressive offering of interdisciplinary and professional development programs taught by the college’s world-class faculty. Accredited by The Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business International (AACSB), the College of Business grants undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral degrees. FAU College of Business emphasizes innovation and entrepreneurism through practical instruction, real-life consulting opportunities, interaction with successful executives, and research efforts conducted at its variety of centers. Centers such as the Adams Center for Entrepreneurship; the Runway at Florida Atlantic; the Research Park at FAU; the WAVE Program; the Madden Center for Value Creation; and the Phil Smith Center for Free Enterprise all offer opportunities to create and test business models, create comprehensive business plans, and obtain external investments to fuel their start-ups. FAU Business has been recognized for outstanding institutional performance by organizations like U.S. News & World Report, The Princeton Review, Financial Times, and Bloomberg Businessweek. Strategically, the College strives to inspire students, faculty, and the regional business community to innovate and make fundamental and positive changes to the way business is conducted. The Director of Advancement for the College of Business at Florida Atlantic University works collaboratively with the Dean, Associate and Assistant Deans, and faculty, and under the supervision of the Vice President and/or an Assistant Vice President for Institutional Advancement. The Director plans, articulates, and implements a comprehensive strategic fundraising plan to meet the educational and research missions and activities of the College of Business and its programs and areas. The Director qualifies, cultivates, solicits, and stewards a portfolio of donors and prospective donors with the inclination and capacity to make significant gifts ($100,000 and greater) to the College of Business at FAU. The successful candidate will experience a commitment to Advancement at the very top from the President; a seasoned, dynamic Vice President of Institutional Advancement with a winning track record; an innovative and committed Dean at the College of Business; and the opportunities and responsibilities appropriate for fundraising leaders to complete Florida Atlantic’s next campaign. Summary of Responsibilities: Develop and implement comprehensive cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship strategies for individual major, legacy, and principal gift prospects assigned. Work both independently and in concert with Institutional Advancement colleagues to implement strategies leading to direct solicitation of gifts of $100,000 and more. Build a strong pipeline of alumni and other prospective donors to expand the portfolio of qualified prospects for gifts of $100,000 and more. Create and execute solicitation and closure strategies for major gifts aligned with the College of Business and University fundraising priorities and campaigns, measured against the attainment of personal metrics associated with the position. Collaborate with the Dean, department chairs, and faculty to identify funding priorities, assess relevance and feasibility for proposed project/priority, and develop and manage comprehensive strategies to secure gifts for selected priorities. Devise individualized involvement/engagement strategies for all prospects using an approach that ensures that most highly rated prospects receive the most attention. Partner with Institutional Advancement’s Legacy Giving Office to devise an overall strategy for cultivating, soliciting, and stewarding planned gift donors. In concert with Institutional Advancement colleagues, oversee the preparation of necessary materials including concept papers, funding proposals, briefings for FAU leadership and board members when necessary, and scheduled stewardship reports, for all assigned prospects. Identify prospects to participate on boards, committees, or other programs that promote the cultivation process. Partner with the Donor Relations and Stewardship Office to ensure appropriate stewardship is provided to donors on existing endowment and current-use funds. Facilitate effective communication between the College of Business and its Centers and programs, and the division of Institutional Advancement. Participate in signature events at the University, within the College, and in the community that provide opportunities for strategic engagement with prospects and donors. Manage the advancement/fundraising function of the College of Business Advisory Board; act as a liaison to the Board and to the Office of Institutional Advancement on policies, procedures, and approvals. In conjunction with the College’s scholarship contacts, oversee that all donor outcomes related to scholarships, such as thank-you notes, event attendance, and in-person visits, are executed in a timely manner. Participate in weekly meetings with the Dean to discuss donors and other fundraising priorities with the College of Business. Supervise a team of advancement and community engagement colleagues in the College of Business. Successful Candidate Will Have the Following Characteristics: Collaborative, goal-oriented, strategic, and highly motivated working style. The ability to demonstrate leadership, take initiative, problem-solve, act independently and as a member of a team, successfully collaborate, handle multiple tasks simultaneously, and prioritize. The ability to demonstrate strategic thinking, good judgment, maturity, and personal integrity. Excellent interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills, and an ability to communicate and collaborate effectively with a diverse campus community including senior administrators, faculty, staff, and students, as well as donors, prospects, alumni, and community leaders. Ability to use tact and diplomacy to handle a broad range of high-level and sensitive situations with diverse personalities, and the ability to adeptly respond to challenges. Able to work beyond traditional work hours and on occasional holidays. Ability to travel as needed and adjust working hours to meet requirements of special tasks and events. Ability to translate academia-speak to diverse audiences. FAU Benefits and Perks If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers: Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more. State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans. State employees  Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF)  program. Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php   Explore Living in Palm Beach County The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: A bachelor’s degree and seven years of fundraising experience, or a master’s degree and five years of fundraising experience, is required. Able to demonstrate measurable success in closing gifts ($100,000 or more) from individual donors, including alumni and friends, and/or institutional donors such as foundations and corporations. Demonstrable experience developing fundraising strategies in partnership with senior academic leadership. Proficiency in using standard computer applications, including word-processing, spreadsheet, CRM software, calendaring, email, and online applications, and a working knowledge of social media. Raiser's Edge experience is helpful. Salary: $165,000 - $180,000. Annually Administrative, Managerial and Professional (AMP) FLSA Exempt College or Department: Division of Institutional Advancement Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday – Friday. This position will require travel and/or work outside of standard business days and hours related to donor activities and engagement. Application Deadline: 2026-10-17 Special Instructions to Applicant: **This recruitment may close without prior notice ** APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Director-of-Advancement--College-of-Medicine_REQ22924": {
      "title": "Director of Advancement, College of Medicine",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-17\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University seeks an experienced fundraising leader to join a relationship-focused, results-oriented, donor-centered advancement team. The Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine is one of the nation's fastest-growing medical schools. We are committed to our core missions of advancing excellence in education and training, research, clinical care, and community engagement.  We are embarking on a bold transformation to evolve from our strong foundation as a community-based medical school into a leading academic health system that advances healthcare through excellence in our core missions. The Director of Advancement for the Schmidt College of Medicine at Florida Atlantic University works collaboratively with the Dean, Associate and Assistant Deans, and faculty, and under the supervision of the Vice President and/or an Assistant Vice President for Institutional Advancement. The Director plans, articulates, and implements a comprehensive strategic fundraising plan to meet the core missions of the Schmidt College of Medicine and its departments, programs, and areas. The Director qualifies, cultivates, solicits, and stewards a portfolio of donors and prospective donors with the inclination and capacity to make significant gifts ($100,000 and greater) to the Schmidt College of Medicine at FAU. The successful candidate will join an institution with a commitment to Advancement at the very top from the President; a seasoned, dynamic Vice President of Institutional Advancement with a winning track record; an innovative Dean committed to philanthropy; and the opportunities and responsibilities appropriate for fundraising leaders to complete Florida Atlantic’s next campaign. Summary of Responsibilities: Develop and implement comprehensive cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship strategies for individual major, legacy, and principal gift prospects assigned. Work both independently and in concert with Institutional Advancement colleagues to implement strategies leading to direct solicitation of gifts of $100,000 and more. Build a strong pipeline of alumni and other prospective donors to expand the portfolio of qualified prospects for gifts of $100,000 and more. Create and execute solicitation and closure strategies for major gifts aligned with the Schmidt College of Medicine and University fundraising priorities and campaigns, measured against the attainment of personal metrics associated with the position. Collaborate with the Dean, department chairs, and faculty to identify funding priorities, assess relevance and feasibility for proposed project/priority, and develop and manage comprehensive strategies to secure gifts for selected priorities. Devise individualized involvement/engagement strategies for all prospects using an approach that ensures that most highly rated prospects receive the most attention. Partner with Institutional Advancement’s Legacy Giving Office to devise an overall strategy for cultivating, soliciting, and stewarding planned gift donors. In concert with Institutional Advancement colleagues, oversee the preparation of necessary materials including concept papers, funding proposals, briefings for FAU leadership and board members when necessary, and scheduled stewardship reports, for all assigned prospects. Identify prospects to participate on boards, committees, or other programs that promote the cultivation process. Partner with the Donor Relations and Stewardship Office to ensure appropriate stewardship is provided to donors on existing endowment and current-use funds. Facilitate effective communication between the Schmidt College of Medicine and the division of Institutional Advancement. Participate in signature events at the University, within the College, and in the community that provide opportunities for strategic engagement with prospects and donors. Manage the advancement/fundraising function of the Schmidt College of Medicine Advisory Board; act as a liaison to the Board and to the Office of Institutional Advancement on policies, procedures, and approvals. In conjunction with the College’s scholarship contacts, oversee that all donor outcomes related to scholarships, such as thank-you notes, event attendance, and in-person visits, are executed in a timely manner. Participate in weekly meetings with the Dean to discuss donors and other fundraising priorities with the Schmidt College of Medicine. Supervise and support a team of advancement and community engagement professionals in the Schmidt College of Medicine responsible for fundraising, donor engagement, and strategic initiatives.​ Successful Candidate Will Have the Following Characteristics: Collaborative, goal-oriented, strategic, and highly motivated working style. The ability to demonstrate leadership, take initiative, problem-solve, act independently and as a member of a team, successfully collaborate, handle multiple tasks simultaneously, and prioritize. The ability to demonstrate strategic thinking, good judgment, maturity, and personal integrity. Excellent interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills, and an ability to communicate and collaborate effectively with a diverse campus community including senior administrators, faculty, staff, and students, as well as donors, prospects, alumni, and community leaders. Ability to use tact and diplomacy to handle a broad range of high-level and sensitive situations with diverse personalities, and the ability to adeptly respond to challenges. Able to work beyond traditional work hours and on occasional holidays. Ability to travel as needed and adjust working hours to meet requirements of special tasks and events. Ability to communicate complex academic and research priorities in ways that resonate with potential donors. FAU Benefits and Perks If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers: Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more. State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans. State employees  Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF)  program. Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php   Explore Living in Palm Beach County The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: A bachelor’s degree and seven years of fundraising experience, or a master’s degree and five years of fundraising experience, is required. Able to demonstrate measurable success in closing gifts ($100,000 or more) from individual donors, including alumni and friends, and/or institutional donors such as foundations and corporations. Demonstrable experience developing fundraising strategies in partnership with senior academic leadership. Proficiency in using standard computer applications, including word-processing, spreadsheet, CRM software, calendaring, email, and online applications, and a working knowledge of social media. Raiser's Edge experience is helpful. Salary: $165,000 - $180,000. Annually Administrative, Managerial and Professional (AMP) FLSA Exempt College or Department: Division of Institutional Advancement Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday – Friday. This position will require travel and/or work outside of standard business days and hours related to donor activities and engagement. Application Deadline: 2026-10-17 Special Instructions to Applicant: **This recruitment may close without prior notice ** APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
