    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Harbor-Branch-HBOI/Postdoctoral-Fellow-HAB_REQ22896": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow HAB",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-16\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The Postdoctoral Fellow will conduct coupled physical-biogeochemical modeling to understand harmful algal blooms (HABs) in subtropical estuaries. The new hire will work with a team of scientists at HBOI and University of Georgia to examine key physical and biogeochemical processes driving the phytoplankton blooms and the selection mechanisms of dominant phytoplankton groups/species. The long-term goals are to predict future changes of water quality, phytoplankton blooms, and ecosystems including seagrass in this region under the influences of human activity and climate change. This position is located at FAU's Harbor Branch campus in Fort Pierce, FL, and is funded by the NOAA ECOHAB program and HBOIF. The appointment will be for two years with possible extension depending on funding availability and job performance. Primary duties and responsibilities: Develops and improves a coupled physical-biogeochemical model for Indian River Lagoon Performs numerical simulations, analysis of the model results, and data analysis Prepares research presentations, manuscripts, and proposals Additional duties and responsibilities: Assists in coordination between modeling, field and lab research teams Participates and assists in field and/or lab work Minimum Qualifications: A Ph.D. from an accredited institution in Marine Science, Oceanography, or closely related fields by time of application. Strong mathematical skills and significant programming experience (e.g. Fortran, Matlab, Python, Linux). Significant experience in numerical modeling and familiar with at least one of the ocean models such as ROMS, POM, and FVCOM. Fundamental knowledge in coastal phytoplankton blooms, biogeochemical cycles, and/or ecosystem dynamics. Salary: $60,000 - $66,000 annually College or Department: Harbor Branch Oceanographic Institute Location: Harbor Branch (HBOI) Work Days and Hours: N/A Application Deadline: 2027-12-31 Special Instructions to Applicant: This is a research or research-related support position. As required by Florida Statutes Section 1010.35, a Foreign Influence Screening may be required. This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: FAU’s Career Page permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. PLEASE NOTE: A maximum of five (5) documents may be attached to your application. If more than five (5) documents are required for submission, please combine additional documents into a single attachment to not exceed the maximum permitted. The site permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. Candidates wishing full consideration are to provide the following: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Research statement Copies of official transcripts Contact information for three references Transcripts: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Facilities-Documentation-Associate_REQ22837": {
      "title": "Facilities Documentation Associate",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-16\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking a Facilities Documentation Associate - Boca Raton, FL. The Facilities Documentation Associate reports to the GIS & Space Data Specialist, the Facilities Documentation Associate serves all University campuses and sites. This is a technical paraprofessional position that supports facilities and infrastructure mapping and documentation by interpreting, capturing, and maintaining accurate facilities and infrastructure records related to buildings, grounds, and utility systems.  This position focuses on the technical review and documentation of civil, utility, and facilities information – including record drawings, as-builts, final construction turnover documentation, and infrastructure asset changes, to ensure that institutional mapping and documentation repositories remain complete, accurate, and current. The role supports updates resulting from both capital projects and operations and maintenance activities and works collaboratively with Design and Construction Services and Operations and Maintenance staff to obtain required technical information for documentation purposes.  The Facilities Documentation Associate plays a key role in maintaining reliable facilities and infrastructure records that support planning, maintenance, compliance, and long-term asset stewardship.  This position is designated as essential personnel.   DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:    Key Responsibilities   Interpret, document, and maintain accurate facilities and infrastructure records for buildings, grounds, and utility systems across all University campuses and sites.  Maintain authoritative infrastructure documentation, including civil, utility, and facilities records, ensuring consistency with approved record drawings, as-built and final construction turnover documentation, and institutional standards.  Provide technical support for the interpretation and documentation of civil engineering drawings, infrastructure documentation and facilities drawings, including site, utility, and building floor plans.  Capture, validate and document infrastructure and spatial changes resulting from capital projects, renovations, and maintenance activities, including review of final construction documentation and equipment schedules, to ensure institutional records remain current and complete.  Identify and coordinate resolution of discrepancies between legacy documentation, submitted records, and field conditions in collaboration with appropriate technical units.  Maintain and update facilities and infrastructure documentation and prepare associated documentation for integration into GIS, space inventory, and related facilities systems.  Work collaboratively with the GIS & Space Data Specialist and coordinate with Design and Construction Services, Operations and Maintenance, and other relevant units to obtain documentation required for accurate recordkeeping.  Provide documentation support for internal reviews, audits, and information requests related to facilities and infrastructure records.  Perform other job-related duties as assigned in support of spatial facilities and infrastructure documentation function.  FAU Benefits and Perks   If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers:  Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more.  State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans.  State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program.  Sick Leave Pool Program.  Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion).  Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day   Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php   Explore Living in Palm Beach County   The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: www.bdb.org/apartments   Minimum Qualifications: Qualifications: • Associate degree in drafting, engineering technology, facilities management, GIS, construction technology, or a related technical field and three (3) years of progressively responsible experience in facilities documentation, infrastructure records, civil/utility drafting, or a closely related technical area OR • High school diploma or equivalent and five (5) years of progressively responsible experience in facilities, infrastructure documentation, drafting, or related technical work demonstrating applied knowledge of civil and utility documentation. • Experience maintaining or updating facilities, infrastructure, utility, or architectural documentation using AutoCAD. Preferred Qualifications: • Experience in higher education, campus environments, or multi-site facilities portfolios. • Familiarity with utilities, site infrastructure, or facilities asset management. • Experience supporting documentation activities across both capital projects and maintenance operations. • Familiarity with facilities mapping or spatial documentation systems is desirable; training may be required to support coordination with GIS, space data and facilities management systems. Physical Requirements: • Ability to move throughout campus and University for site and field visits, and surveys. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES REQUIRED: Technical Knowledge • Utility documentation practices, infrastructure record standards, and campus utility systems sufficient to interpret and maintain facilities and infrastructure records. • Facilities and infrastructure documentation management practices, including record maintenance, version control, and documentation lifecycle processes. • Civil engineering and utility drawing conventions. • As-built, record drawing and construction turnover standards. • Building floor plans and related facilities drawings. • Asset documentation and lifecycle awareness. Technical Skills • Proficiency in AutoCAD sufficient to interpret, update, maintain, and revise facilities and infrastructure documentation based on approved record drawings, as-built documentation, and field verification activities. • Ability to translate engineering documentation into structured spatial and asset records. • Ability to conduct field verification activities, including site observations, photographic documentation, and comparison of field conditions with existing records. • Strong attention to technical detail and documentation accuracy. Analytical & Coordination Skills • Ability to identify inconsistencies across documentation sources. • Clear communication with technical and non-technical stakeholders. • Methodical recordkeeping and version control practices. Salary: $60,000.00 to $65,000.00 per year College or Department: Facilities Management: Design and Construction Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Application Deadline: 2026-10-28 Special Instructions to Applicant: **This position does not offer any employment-based immigration sponsorship now or in the future. **Unrestricted work authorization required at all times. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accomodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Law-Enforcement-Officer-3_REQ22855": {
      "title": "Law Enforcement Officer-3",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-16\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking a Law Enforcement Officer. - Boca Raton, FL. The Law Enforcement Officer is here to keep our community safe and believes in the benefits and openness of transparency in policing. We want everyone to understand who we are, what our policies are and why they exist, and how Florida Atlantic Police Officers train and prepare for emergency situations. FAPD officers train annually on defensive tactics, firearms, taser and de-escalation techniques. Officers participate in two active shooter scenarios, a department-wide and a multi-agency large scale scenario. Monthly officers complete training on policies, procedures and state law. Summary Of Responsibilities: Provides safety and security presence for university property by application of conscientious vehicle, golf cart and foot patrol functions on a rotating shift basis. Performs duties as a gate attendant for HBOI access control at the main entrance. Communicates regularly with HBOI Human Resources, employees and associates regarding access to visitors. Responds and investigates crimes reported, vehicle accidents, medical emergencies, fires, safety hazards, fire and security alarms received and all other occurrences within the scope of the department’s responsibilities and mission. Prepares departmental, county and state forms as required. Enforces applicable University policies, traffic and parking services regulations, State Criminal Code and Statutes governing state traffic laws. Issues appropriate citations, student referrals and/or effects arrests as necessary in the performance of these law enforcement duties. Renders informational services to members of the University community and visitors, assists motorists experiencing vehicle problems, provides security escort services, and handles traffic control and parking directions for a variety of educational, cultural and athletic events held on campus. Conducts security and safety checks of university buildings, housing and university grounds. Secures and opens buildings at scheduled times and upon request of authorized persons. Provides a university crime prevention function during security rounds by advising department of unsafe or unsecured conditions observed. FAU Benefits and Perks If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers: Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more. State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans. State employees  Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF)  program. Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php   Explore Living in Palm Beach County The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: Minimum Qualification High school diploma or equivalent and one year of law enforcement experience required. Must meet the requirements of Chapter 943 of the Florida Statutes. Must be at least 19 years of age and a U.S. citizen and be able to pass physical and psychological examinations, a rigorous background investigation and not have been convicted of a felony or misdemeanor. Ability to work in stressful and sometimes hazardous conditions. Ability to safely operate a patrol vehicle and emergency equipment. Ability to grasp criminal and traffic laws and to make sound decisions. Ability to exercise restraint and tact with all members of the University community and the general public. Ability to physically and mentally satisfy state and departmental training requirements. Ability to effectively work without direct supervision. Ability to work well with fellow officers: Teamwork concept. A valid driver’s license is required. Salary: $26.06 per hour. Non-Exempt Support Personnel (SP) College or Department: University Police Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Hours and workdays may vary and include day, evening, overnight, weekend, and holiday shifts based on operational needs. Application Deadline: 2026-10-12 Special Instructions to Applicant: VETERANS’ PREFERENCE: Applicants may claim Veterans’ Preference on their application. The applicant claiming preference is responsible for providing required documentation at the time of making an application in Workday for a vacant position, or prior to the closing date of the vacancy announcement. If an applicant qualifies for Veterans' Preference and the SP position, they are shown preference by the guarantee of an interview. Veterans’ Preference does not guarantee a job. For additional information, please visit https://www.fau.edu/jobs/resources/veterans/. For assistance, please contact Recruitment Services at empl@fau.edu. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Dean-of-Academic-Success_REQ22799": {
      "title": "Dean of Academic Success",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University seeks a strategic, collaborative, and innovative leader to serve as Dean of Academic Success. Reporting to the Senior Associate Vice President for Strategic Planning and Student Success, the Dean serves as a university-wide leader responsible for advancing academic support, advising strategy, enrollment-connected academic planning, and high-impact educational practices. The Dean provides leadership for initiatives that promote student success, defined as student retention, academic progression toward timely degree completion, and readiness for professional or continued educational pathways. The overall goal of the position is to improve undergraduate and graduate student outcomes. This role provides leadership for cross-functional initiatives that strengthen the connection between enrollment pipelines, academic support structures, educational experiences, and student outcomes. The Dean will drive change, empower faculty and staff, and align institutional efforts with university priorities, Board of Trustees’ direction, and state-level expectations, including those of the Florida Board of Governors. This role may include leadership or oversight for units and functions such as: Academic support and learning assistance programs University advising services, advising systems, and academic coaching General education oversight and related academic standards Assessment of student success initiatives and progression supports Undergraduate and graduate academic support coordination Undergraduate research, fellowships, honors, and related initiatives, as assigned Additional responsibilities assigned through Academic Affairs or the Provost’s Office Primary Responsibilities Strategic Leadership and Institutional Partnership Serve as a senior strategic leader and principal partner to the Senior Associate Vice President for Strategic Planning and Student Success. Lead and advance a university-wide vision for academic success that connects enrollment strategy, academic support, advising, progression, retention, and graduation outcomes. Serve as a thought leader on integrating AI and emerging technology into the curriculum to ensure students build essential career skills. Develop and implement cross-functional initiatives that improve student achievement for undergraduate and graduate students – including through the Enrollment Management Oversight Committee and collaborations with the Graduate College. Leadership of Academic Success Portfolio Provide direct leadership and administrative oversight for centralized academic success and support functions. Oversee university-wide standards for academic advising, systems, coordination, and student support structures, while partnering with colleges on seamless student-facing experiences. Direct and strengthen the university’s approach to general education oversight, broad curricular policy coordination, and related academic standards. Oversee high-impact practices and collaborate with other units on experiential learning opportunities. Ensure academic support and advising strategies are aligned to the needs of various student populations, including first-year students, transfer students, student-athletes, ROTC students, high-achieving students, and other key populations. Collaboration with Colleges and Academic Affairs Serve as a bridge-builder across Academic Affairs and related divisions to foster collaboration around institutional student success priorities. Partner with the colleges in ways that support and complement shared governance over discipline-specific curriculum, program content, and major-specific advising. Support broad academic policy development and implementation through university-level committees and governance processes. Operational and Administrative Leadership Provide leadership for budget, planning, staffing, and organizational development across the academic success portfolio. Support university-level academic processes and designated responsibilities, which may include matters such as academic policy support, academic integrity appeals, grade grievances, or related functions assigned through the Provost’s Office. Advance a culture of innovation, accountability, collaboration, and continuous improvement. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled; however, review of applications will begin September 28, and candidates are encouraged to apply by that date to ensure full consideration. Questions regarding this position may be directed to provost@fau.edu or 561-297-3062, Attn: Geoffrey Johnson, Assistant Vice President for Academic Operations and Initiatives, FAU Office of the Provost. Minimum Qualifications: Required Qualifications: • Terminal degree from an accredited institution. • A distinguished record of achievement and professional credentials consistent with tenure and a faculty appointment. • Significant senior-level leadership experience in higher education, preferably in academic affairs, student success, advising, enrollment-connected academic planning, or related areas. • A commitment to innovation and professional development for high-performing teams. • Demonstrated ability to build productive partnerships with faculty, deans, executive leaders, and administrative units. • Experience using data, assessment, and evidence to inform strategy, planning, and decision-making. • Strong communication, organizational, and change leadership skills. Preferred Qualifications: • Experience in a large public university or multi-campus environment. • Knowledge of state university system priorities, accountability frameworks, and governing board expectations. • Experience overseeing or partnering on general education, broad academic policy, centralized advising systems, or university-level curricular processes. • Experience supporting both undergraduate and graduate student success initiatives. Salary: $225,000. - $275,000. College or Department: Academic Affairs Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: N/A Application Deadline: 2027-01-31 Special Instructions to Applicant: This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: FAU’s Career Page permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. PLEASE NOTE: A maximum of five (5) documents may be attached to your application. If more than five (5) documents are required for submission, please combine additional documents into a single attachment to not exceed the maximum permitted. The site permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. Candidates wishing full consideration are to provide the following: a cover letter and curriculum vitae. Transcripts: The selected candidate for this position is required to submit an official transcript sent directly from the institution for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Similarly, for degrees from outside the United States, the evaluation by an organization belonging to the National Association of Credential Evaluation (NACES), with an indication of the documents the evaluation was prepared from (official transcripts, diplomas, dissertation abstracts) is required for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Transcripts must be issued to Florida Atlantic University, not to the individual applicant. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Medical-Educator--Assistant-Professor-Associate-Professor-Professor-_REQ22281": {
      "title": "Medical Educator (Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/Professor)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine at Florida Atlantic University seeks a medical educator to teach primarily in the basic science curriculum during the first two years of the MD program and serve in other potential roles within the College.  The basic science courses engage students in active, participatory learning that integrates medical knowledge, clinical skills, habits of self-directed learning, and diagnostic reasoning skills with a small group, problem-based learning (PBL) approach.  Student activities include case-based discussions, workshops, lectures, and laboratory work. Our integrated basic science curriculum is structured by organ systems and clinical presentations, ensuring that basic sciences and clinical skills are concurrently taught during the first two years. Essential duties for this position may include, but are not limited to, the following:  Create and present lectures and other educational sessions that meet established learning objectives and collaborate with course directors and faculty to ensure integration of material across courses. Serve as a facilitator for small group problem-based learning sessions and an instructor for applicable laboratory sessions.   Assist with preparation and administration of exams and other assessments as requested. Participate in course grading committees and assist with course remediation as needed. Direct or co-direct one or more designated curriculum courses, threads, programs and/or content areas. Teach in other areas of the curriculum aligned with experience. Examples include classroom and small group teaching in the Year 1 and 2 Foundations of Medicine courses, the Year 3 Synthesis and Transition course and Academic Half-Day sessions, and the Year 4 Transition to Residency course.  As opportunities arise, serve as an instructor in COM graduate programs in fields of expertise. Participate in faculty/facilitator meetings and faculty development sessions. Advise and mentor medical students as well as graduate students and residents, as applicable. Actively engage in continuous quality improvement efforts to ensure that the curriculum meets LCME accreditation standards. Serve on College of Medicine and University committees as required or requested. Conduct scholarly work related to medical education, applicable basic science or clinical disciplines, or another area of interest. Minimum Qualifications: • Terminal degree (PhD, MD, or equivalent degree) in a related basic science field or clinical discipline, such as Biochemistry, Physiology, Pathology, Anatomy, Histology, Embryology, Microbiology, or Molecular Biology and credentials that merit appointment at the rank of assistant professor or higher. • Candidates with an MD or equivalent degree may require a Florida medical license or qualifications for licensure and board certification, depending on scope of professional activities. • Exceptional time management, the ability to be flexible, adaptable, and manage multiple demands and effectively communicate (oral and written) with a wide range of university stakeholders. • Possess a high level of professionalism, independence and dependability. Preferred Qualifications: • A minimum of 3 years of experience teaching basic sciences at the undergraduate medical education level. • Experience in curriculum development using innovative approaches to education, including use of educational technology. • Expertise in assessment of learner performance. • Experience directing a course or curriculum. • A track record of scholarship including invited lectures, enduring materials, peer-reviewed publications and/or grant-funded projects. • Experience with LCME accreditation or other accreditation organizations. • Experience with quality improvement and educational program evaluation. Salary: Commensurate with Experience College or Department: Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: N/A Application Deadline: 2026-12-01 Special Instructions to Applicant: This recruitment has been reopened; all previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: FAU’s Career Page permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. PLEASE NOTE: A maximum of five (5) documents may be attached to your application. If more than five (5) documents are required for submission, please combine additional documents into a single attachment to not exceed the maximum permitted. The site permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. Candidates wishing full consideration are to provide the following: a cover letter and curriculum vitae. Transcripts: The selected candidate for this position is required to submit an official transcript sent directly from the institution for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Similarly, for degrees from outside the United States, the evaluation by an organization belonging to the National Association of Credential Evaluation (NACES), with an indication of the documents the evaluation was prepared from (official transcripts, diplomas, dissertation abstracts) is required for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Transcripts must be issued to Florida Atlantic University, not to the individual applicant. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Surgery-Clerkship-Director--Assistant-Professor-Associate-Professor-Full-Professor-_REQ22701": {
      "title": "Surgery Clerkship Director (Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/Full Professor)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine at Florida Atlantic University seeks an accomplished surgeon-educator to serve as Surgery Clerkship Director, reporting to the Chair of the Department of Surgery with a secondary academic reporting relationship to the Associate Dean for Medical Education. This leadership role provides strategic direction and oversight for the required Surgery Clerkship within the College’s longitudinal integrated clinical curriculum, ensuring excellence in surgical education, student assessment, faculty engagement, and clinical learning experiences across affiliated training sites. The Surgery Clerkship Director will work closely with Undergraduate Medical Education leadership, faculty, residents, and affiliated clinical partners to advance curriculum innovation, continuous quality improvement, and compliance with LCME accreditation standards. This position includes a 0.5 FTE educational and administrative appointment and a 0.5 FTE clinical faculty appointment, with the expectation of maintaining an active surgical practice that supports outstanding patient care, bedside teaching, learner mentorship, and surgical resident education. The successful candidate will have a track record demonstrating a commitment to fostering academic excellence, professionalism, and student success while helping prepare the next generation of physicians. Primary Responsibilities The Surgery Clerkship Director’s primary responsibilities include but are not limited to the following: Provide overall leadership, administration, and oversight of the required surgery clerkship across all affiliated clinical training sites. Direct the supervision of medical students during their assigned surgical clerkship experiences throughout the Medical and Surgical Sciences Longitudinal Integrated Clerkship by: Providing direct clinical supervision and bedside teaching at the Director's primary clinical practice site(s). Maintaining regular communication with site directors, clerkship coordinators, preceptors, and core teaching faculty to ensure consistency in educational experiences and student assessment. Attend monthly Clerkship Director meetings and any additional meetings necessary to review student performance and curriculum implementation issues. Periodically visit all clinical teaching sites for the surgery clerkship to observe and ensure high quality and positive learning environments. Enhance and continuously refine the surgery clerkship curriculum, in collaboration with the Assistant Dean for Clinical Curriculum, in accordance with LCME accreditation standards and institutional educational objectives. Deliver surgery lectures to various levels of medical students each year and facilitate Diagnosis & Reasoning (DR) rounds for the clerkship students at the College of Medicine during in-person weekly academic half day. Develop, organize, and oversee the annual schedule of didactic lectures and educational activities, ensuring appropriate faculty participation and instructional quality. Oversee student assessment and evaluation, including preparation and review of narrative evaluations and timely submission of final clerkship grades in coordination with the Surgery Clerkship grading committee. Prepare all student narrative comments for the surgery clerkship that will be included in the students’ Medical Student Performance Evaluation (MSPE/Dean’s Letter). Provide timely formative and summative feedback to students regarding clinical performance, professionalism, medical knowledge, technical skills, clinical reasoning, and achievement of clerkship learning objectives. Serve as a feedback coach to provide ongoing formative feedback to students, including review of goals achieved, strengths, adequacy of patient load and experiences, and areas for continuing work. Develop individualized performance improvement and/or remediation plans for students demonstrating academic or professional deficiencies, establish measurable goals and timelines, and monitor progress, in collaboration with Year 3 Curriculum Director/Co-Director, and communicate outcomes to the Assistant Dean for Clinical Curriculum, the Associate Dean for Medical Education, Chair of the Department of Surgery, and the Medical Student Promotions and Professional Standards Committee, when appropriate. Regularly evaluate the adequacy of clinical experiences, patient volume, faculty teaching effectiveness, and educational resources across all clerkship sites. Provide regular reports to the Chair of the Department of Surgery regarding clerkship performance, curricular initiatives, faculty participation, student outcomes, accreditation issues, and resource needs. Serve as a mentor and career advisor to medical students pursuing careers in surgery, including guidance regarding residency applications, career planning, research opportunities, and professional development. Work directly with FAU General Surgery residents during the clinical portion of the appointment and promote integration of clerkship students into the resident educational experience whenever appropriate. Serve as an active educational leader within the FAU General Surgery Residency Program by participating in: Clinical Competency Committee (CCC) Annual Program Evaluation Committee (APEC) Resident didactic education Surgical skills laboratories Residency recruitment and applicant interviews Prepare letters of recommendation for students applying to Surgery residency programs and any other letters of recommendation requested by students to support their success (ex. research opportunities, away rotations, scholarships), as appropriate. Participate in ongoing curriculum evaluation and quality improvement initiatives by analyzing clerkship outcomes, student feedback, faculty evaluations, and national best practices in surgical education, and implementing curricular improvements as indicated. Build and maintain collaborative relationships with faculty, site directors, and educational leaders at each affiliated training site while proactively identifying and resolving issues affecting the quality of the clerkship. Provide faculty development and constructive feedback to teaching faculty to enhance the educational experience, teaching effectiveness, learner assessment, and mentorship of medical students. Complete annual evaluations for Surgery affiliate faculty who teach and mentor medical students for review by the Associate Dean for Medical Education and the College's Committee on Appointments and Promotions, which oversees affiliate faculty appointments, reappointments, and promotions. Participate in LCME accreditation preparation, documentation, and site visits as requested. Assist in the development, implementation, and evaluation of Objective Structured Clinical Examinations (OSCEs), simulation-based education, and other innovative instructional activities within the FAU College of Medicine. Perform additional administrative, educational, and departmental responsibilities as assigned by the Chair of the Department of Surgery. Clinical Practice Expectations The Surgery Clerkship Director is expected to maintain an active clinical surgical practice within the Department of Surgery. The incumbent must demonstrate a sustained commitment to excellence in patient care while providing a diverse and meaningful clinical learning environment for medical students and surgical residents. The clinical practice should provide sufficient patient volume and operative experience to support high-quality bedside teaching, clinical supervision, and mentorship of learners. The Clerkship Director is expected to model professionalism, evidence-based surgical care, and effective interdisciplinary collaboration, while integrating medical students into appropriate clinical and operative experiences consistent with the educational objectives of the Surgery Clerkship. Overall Expectations The Surgery Clerkship Director is expected to demonstrate excellence in clinical teaching, educational leadership, curriculum development, faculty mentorship, student advising, and continuous quality improvement. The successful candidate will serve as a key educational leader within both the Department of Surgery and the College of Medicine while fostering a culture of professionalism, accountability, academic excellence, and innovation in surgical education. Minimum Qualifications: • MD, DO, or equivalent terminal degree from an accredited institution and the credentials that merit appointment at the rank of assistant, associate, or full professor are required. • Florida medical license or eligibility for Florida licensure and board eligibility or certification in applicable clinical specialty is required. • At least 2 years of experience in undergraduate medical school education is preferred. • Exceptional interpersonal communication skills required. • Exceptional writing skills required. • Strong ethical and professional conduct is required. • The ability to effectively communicate with a wide range of stakeholders and learners from varied backgrounds is required. • Exceptional time management, adaptability, flexibility, and the ability to manage multiple demands are required. Salary: Commensurate with Experience College or Department: Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: N/A Application Deadline: 2026-12-01 Special Instructions to Applicant: This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: FAU’s Career Page permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. PLEASE NOTE: A maximum of five (5) documents may be attached to your application. If more than five (5) documents are required for submission, please combine additional documents into a single attachment to not exceed the maximum permitted. The site permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. Candidates wishing full consideration are to provide the following: a cover letter and curriculum vitae. Transcripts: The selected candidate for this position is required to submit an official transcript sent directly from the institution for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Similarly, for degrees from outside the United States, the evaluation by an organization belonging to the National Association of Credential Evaluation (NACES), with an indication of the documents the evaluation was prepared from (official transcripts, diplomas, dissertation abstracts) is required for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Transcripts must be issued to Florida Atlantic University, not to the individual applicant. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Associate-Dean-for-Academic-Programs_REQ22683": {
      "title": "Associate Dean for Academic Programs",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Associate Dean for Academic Programs College of Business The College of Business invites applications for a full-time, 12-month, non-tenure-track position as Associate Dean for Academic Programs. Reporting to the Dean, the Associate Dean provides leadership for academic programs, AACSB accreditation, and continuous improvement systems, with primary responsibility for the strategic management of accreditation processes. Duties include oversight of assurance of learning, faculty qualifications, curating a centralized record of intellectual contributions, and accreditation reporting; coordination of data systems supporting continuous improvement; and leadership of faculty credentialing and instructional resource alignment to maintain compliance with AACSB standards. The position also oversees academic advising and student services, manages student academic issues, and collaborates with faculty and academic leadership on program development, assessment, and initiatives that enhance student success and academic quality. The role includes limited teaching responsibilities in one of the College’s academic departments, service to the College and University, and maintenance of scholarly activity consistent with AACSB Scholarly Academic (SA) status. Minimum Qualifications: • Earned a doctorate from an AACSB-accredited business school • An established research portfolio to have and maintain AACSB Scholarly Academic (SA) status • Minimum of five (5) years of academic administrative experience, preferably at the Assistant or Associate Dean level • Significant experience with AACSB accreditation (including assurance of learning, strategic deployment of faculty, and faculty credentialing) • Experience overseeing academic advising and related student academic support services and personnel in those areas Salary: Commensurate with Experience College or Department: College of Business Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: N/A Application Deadline: 2026-12-01 Special Instructions to Applicant: This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: FAU’s Career Page permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. PLEASE NOTE: A maximum of five (5) documents may be attached to your application. If more than five (5) documents are required for submission, please combine additional documents into a single attachment to not exceed the maximum permitted. The site permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. Candidates wishing full consideration are to provide the following: a letter of application, CV, and contact information for three references. Transcripts: The selected candidate for this position is required to submit an official transcript sent directly from the institution for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Similarly, for degrees from outside the United States, the evaluation by an organization belonging to the National Association of Credential Evaluation (NACES), with an indication of the documents the evaluation was prepared from (official transcripts, diplomas, dissertation abstracts) is required for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Transcripts must be issued to Florida Atlantic University, not to the individual applicant. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Associate-Dean-for-Medical-Education--Associate-Professor-Full-Professor-_REQ22692-1": {
      "title": "Associate Dean for Medical Education (Associate Professor/Full Professor)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: WittKieffer is proud to partner with The Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine at Florida Atlantic University in their search for the next Associate Dean for Medial Education, a key faculty leadership role overseeing undergraduate medical education, including curriculum, assessment, accreditation, and educational innovation. Florida Atlantic University (Florida Atlantic) is a public research university with ten colleges, 30,000 students, and six campuses spanning more than 100 miles of coastline. The University has seen remarkable growth in its programs and reputation in just the last few years, including doubling research expenditures, enrolling an all-time high number of National Merit Scholars, setting new records for private gifts to the FAU Foundation, increasing graduation and academic progress rates, and raising the profile of Florida Atlantic's athletics program. For the first time in 2026, Florida Atlantic was named a \"Top 100 Public University\" by U.S. News & World Report , rising from No. 103 in last year’s ranking of the nation’s best universities. Created to address the state's healthcare needs, the Schmidt College of Medicine is a community-based medical school that admitted its first class of students in 2011. The College includes 175 faculty (103 full-time and 72 part-time), 1,274 affiliate faculty members, 326 medical students, 181 residents and fellows, and 70 graduate students in biomedical science. Five local hospitals from top healthcare systems in the region, namely Baptist Health and Tenet Health, serve as key partners in undergraduate medical education (UME) and form the Graduate Medical Education (GME) Consortium, which offers residency and fellowship programs. The College is also affiliated with Cleveland Clinic Florida, HCA, and local behavioral health medical centers. The College also has a faculty practice plan, Florida Atlantic Medical Group, and is home to the Max Planck Florida Institute for Neuroscience, offering outstanding research and educational opportunities for faculty and students. The College annually provides approximately 400 students with a variety of educational offerings, including an M.D. program, an M.D./Ph.D. program, M.S. and Ph.D. degree programs in Biomedical Sciences, and graduate certificates. Reporting to the Vice Dean for Medical Education, the Associate Dean for Medical Education will provide strategic leadership and oversight for the College of Medicine's integrated four-year undergraduate medical education program. This highly visible leader will guide the continued evolution of an innovative, learner-centered curriculum, ensuring seamless integration across the pre-clinical and clinical years while advancing emerging areas of medical education such as health systems science, artificial intelligence, nutrition, and point-of-care ultrasound. The Associate Dean will oversee curriculum quality, assessment, accreditation readiness, and continuous quality improvement efforts; mentor and support course and clerkship directors; and foster collaboration among faculty, academic leaders, and community-based clinical partners. As a key ambassador for the College, the Associate Dean will cultivate strong relationships with health systems, physician groups, and community stakeholders to expand and sustain high-quality clinical education opportunities in an increasingly competitive environment. The successful candidate will bring the vision, innovation, and relationship-building skills necessary to support the College's long-term growth, enhance educational excellence, and prepare the medical education enterprise for future expansion. An M.D. or D.O. degree from an accredited institution is required, along with completion of a U.S.-accredited residency program and credentials that merit appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor. Candidates must be board certified or board eligible in their specialty, hold a current U.S. medical license, and be eligible for Florida licensure. Significant leadership experience in undergraduate medical education, curriculum development and innovation, faculty development, and accreditation is required. All applications, nominations, and inquiries are invited. Applications can be submitted through the WittKieffer Candidate Portal . Applicants should submit, as separate documents, a CV or résumé and a letter of interest that addresses the themes outlined in the leadership profile . WittKieffer is assisting Florida Atlantic University in this search. For additional questions, please contact Megan Welch through the office of Charlotte Harris via email at charris@wittkiffer.com . Minimum Qualifications: An M.D. or D.O. degree from an accredited institution is required, along with completion of a U.S.-accredited residency program and credentials that merit appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor. Candidates must be board certified or board eligible in their specialty, hold a current U.S. medical license, and be eligible for Florida licensure. Significant leadership experience in undergraduate medical education, curriculum development and innovation, faculty development, and accreditation is required. Salary: Commensurate with Experience College or Department: Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: N/A Application Deadline: 2026-11-30 Special Instructions to Applicant: This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: All applications, nominations, and inquiries are invited. Applications can be submitted through the WittKieffer Candidate Portal. Applicants should submit, as separate documents, a CV or résumé and a letter of interest that addresses the themes outlined in the leadership profile. WittKieffer is assisting Florida Atlantic University in this search. Transcripts: The selected candidate for this position is required to submit an official transcript sent directly from the institution for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Similarly, for degrees from outside the United States, the evaluation by an organization belonging to the National Association of Credential Evaluation (NACES), with an indication of the documents the evaluation was prepared from (official transcripts, diplomas, dissertation abstracts) is required for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Transcripts must be issued to Florida Atlantic University, not to the individual applicant. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Artificial-Intelligence-in-Medicine---Assistant--Associate--Full-Professor_REQ22638": {
      "title": "Artificial Intelligence in Medicine – Assistant/ Associate/ Full Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The Florida Atlantic University Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine’s, Department of Population Health, is recruiting a visionary faculty member in Artificial Intelligence in Medicine to develop and lead transformative AI-driven initiatives that advance population health, health equity, healthcare delivery, biomedical and community-engaged research. This role offers the opportunity to advance AI applications, machine learning, data science and predictive analytics to address complex public health challenges, improve health outcomes, optimize healthcare systems, enhance biomedical research, innovate clinical research, and develop next-generation graduate and medical education. The successful candidate will serve as a catalyst for cross-disciplinary collaboration, advancing discovery, and improving health outcomes on a broad scale.  The mission of the Schmidt College of Medicine as a community-based medical school is to advance the health and well-being of our community by training future generations of humanistic clinicians and scientists and translating discoveries to patient-centered care. We are committed to providing educational programs that enable our trainees to become active, self-directed, lifelong learners who understand the centrality of collaborative relationships in healthcare research and delivery. We are looking for someone with visionary thinking and a passion for ultimately advancing scientific knowledge and healthcare delivery. The successful candidate will lead and contribute to cutting-edge research, education, and strategic initiatives at the intersection of artificial intelligence, population health, public health, healthcare delivery, and health services research. Key Responsibilities Research & Innovation Collaborate with researchers throughout the College and University to integrate AI into ongoing translational and clinical projects. Contributes to basic and applied research activities and authors scientific publications, technical and agency reports, and patent preparations. Contribute to institutional AI strategic efforts. Develop, lead, and sustain a competitive, externally funded research program (e.g., NIH, NSF, DoD, industry) applying AI/ML methodologies across cutting edge research including observational, clinical, community-based, health services research projects and health outcomes research. Disseminate findings in high-impact journals and at national and/or international conferences. Graduate Education & Curriculum Development Design, implement, and evaluate AI-focused coursework for graduate, medical, and health professional education. Mentor College of Medicine graduate students, medical students, residents, postdocs, and faculty in the development, utilization and policies of AI methodologies in healthcare, clinical, population health, public health, or biomedical research settings. Embed AI modules into existing core and elective courses in the College of Medicine. Serve as a resource for developing new educational programs in the College of Medicine. College-wide Service & Collaboration Serve as an AI resource for faculty and researchers, offering expertise and guidance on data science integration across departments. Partner with program directors to identify AI integration opportunities in existing and future graduate curricula. Contribute to departmental, college, and university committees, and participate in strategic AI-related initiatives and help shape the College’s AI strategy. Build and sustain partnerships with industry, government agencies, and academic collaborators to foster AI-driven research, training, and innovation. Collaborate with clinical partners to develop learning health systems initiatives that narrow the gap between evidence and practice. Minimum Qualifications: • Ph.D., M.D., or equivalent degree or experience in applying artificial intelligence, machine learning, or advanced analytics in healthcare, clinical, population health, public health, or biomedical research settings. • Demonstrated AI and/or machine learning expertise with relevance to biomedical, public health, or clinical challenges. • Strong research publication record and proven (for senior roles) or potential (for junior roles) success in obtaining external funding, publications, and successful mentoring of junior faculty, postdoctoral fellows, and/or graduate students. • Commitment to interdisciplinary collaboration and educational excellence. • Working knowledge of ethical, regulatory, privacy, and governance considerations related to the use of AI in healthcare and biomedical research, including data security, bias mitigation, and responsible AI practices. • Experience working with healthcare data sources, such as electronic health records (EHRs), claims data, registries, clinical research datasets, or population health databases. Preferred Qualifications • Experience developing, implementing, evaluating, or advising on AI governance frameworks, policies, standards, or best practices within healthcare, public health, academic medical centers, government agencies, or healthcare organizations. • Experience applying AI and machine learning methodologies to public health, population health management, health equity, healthcare operations, quality improvement, or community health initiatives. • Demonstrated success translating AI innovations into real-world clinical, public health, or healthcare delivery environments. • Experience collaborating with healthcare systems, public health agencies, community organizations, or other external stakeholders on AI-driven initiatives. • Expertise in emerging areas of AI in healthcare, including generative AI, large language models, clinical decision support, predictive analytics, precision medicine, digital health, and learning health systems. • Experience evaluating the ethical, legal, regulatory, and societal implications of AI technologies in healthcare and public health settings. • Knowledge of federal and state policies, guidance, and evolving best practices related to the deployment of AI in healthcare and public health environments. • Documented success in cross-disciplinary collaboration and research between basic science and clinical faculty. • Engagement in curriculum development or AI educational programming in health sciences. Salary: Commensurate with Experience College or Department: Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: N/A Application Deadline: 2026-11-30 Special Instructions to Applicant: This is a research or research-related support position. As required by Florida Statutes Section 1010.35, a Foreign Influence Screening may be required. This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: FAU’s Career Page permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. PLEASE NOTE: A maximum of five (5) documents may be attached to your application. If more than five (5) documents are required for submission, please combine additional documents into a single attachment to not exceed the maximum permitted. The site permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. Candidates wishing full consideration are to provide the following: a cover letter and curriculum vitae. Transcripts: The selected candidate for this position is required to submit an official transcript sent directly from the institution for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Similarly, for degrees from outside the United States, the evaluation by an organization belonging to the National Association of Credential Evaluation (NACES), with an indication of the documents the evaluation was prepared from (official transcripts, diplomas, dissertation abstracts) is required for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Transcripts must be issued to Florida Atlantic University, not to the individual applicant. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Clinical---Off-Campus-Location-COM-use-only/General-Psychiatry--Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor-_REQ22052-1": {
      "title": "General Psychiatry (Assistant/Associate/Full Professor)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU on its race to excellence. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The Schmidt College of Medicine seeks a dynamic and collaborative clinical faculty member at the rank of Assistant/Associate/Full Professor to serve as an attending physician, within FAU Medicine- Psychiatry Residency. The mission of the Schmidt College of Medicine as a community-based medical school is to advance the health and well-being of our community by training future generations of humanistic clinicians and scientists and translating discovery to patient-centered care. We are committed to providing educational programs, in partnership with our hospital affiliates, that enable our medical students and residents to become active, self-directed, life-long learners; equip our graduates to effectively treat the patients that they are most likely to encounter in their practices; produce graduates with the knowledge, skills, attitudes, and self-awareness required to practice effective, humanistic, patient-centered, evidence-based medicine; emphasize the centrality of collaborative relationships in the provision of the highest quality comprehensive health care; and foster and value collaboration among medical specialties, and between academic medicine and community health care professionals. The General Psychiatry, Assistant/Associate/Full Professor will have the following specific responsibilities: Deliver evidenced-based, best-practice driven psychiatric care. Supervise residents in the development of treatment plans and care pathways to provide personalized care addressing patient needs based on professional practice guidelines and scientific evidence. Provider will maintain close communication with the clinic/hospital healthcare team and provide relevant instruction to care team members as appropriate. Organize multi-disciplinary conferences with appropriate care team. Collaborate with community organizations to support holistic patient care. Discuss findings as needed with collaborating physicians, consulting staff, and medical service providers. Assess patient care needs and monitor patient satisfaction. Perform resident and medical student evaluations as appropriate. Provide a practice environment that encourages a team culture and response to the provision of patient care services. Follow College of Medicine organizational protocols, policies, and procedures. Ensure compliance with all pertinent laws and regulations including the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act (HIPAA). Perform other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Required •  M.D. or D.O. from an accredited institution and credentials that merit appointment at the appropriate rank. •  Florida medical license or eligibility for licensure, and active or eligible certification by the American Board of Psychiatry and Neurology (ABPN). •  The ability to effectively communicate with students, residents, fellows and employees from various backgrounds is required.   Preferred •  Experience with ACGME accreditation, curriculum design, and competency based evaluation. •  Record of scholarly activity and participation in academic psychiatry organizations. Salary: Commensurate with Experience College or Department: Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine Location: Clinical - Off Campus Location (COM use only) Work Days and Hours: N/A Application Deadline: 2026-10-16 Special Instructions to Applicant: This recruitment has been reopened; all previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: FAU’s Career Page permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. PLEASE NOTE: A maximum of five (5) documents may be attached to your application. If more than five (5) documents are required for submission, please combine additional documents into a single attachment to not exceed the maximum permitted. The site permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. Candidates wishing full consideration are to provide the following: a cover letter and curriculum vitae. Transcripts: The selected candidate for this position is required to submit an official transcript sent directly from the institution for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Similarly, for degrees from outside the United States, the evaluation by an organization belonging to the National Association of Credential Evaluation (NACES), with an indication of the documents the evaluation was prepared from (official transcripts, diplomas, dissertation abstracts) is required for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Transcripts must be issued to Florida Atlantic University, not to the individual applicant. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Clinical---Off-Campus-Location-COM-use-only/Program-Director--Psychiatry-Residency--Associate-Professor-Full-Professor-_REQ21835": {
      "title": "Program Director, Psychiatry Residency (Associate Professor/Full Professor)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU on its race to excellence. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The FAU Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine seeks a highly skilled and motivated Psychiatry Residency Program Director (PD) to join our dynamic team. The PD for the Psychiatry Residency Program will provide visionary leadership, strategic direction, and administrative oversight for an Accreditation Council for Graduate Medical Education (ACGME) accredited training program in Psychiatry. The PD is responsible for ensuring full compliance with all ACGME requirements, advancing excellence in graduate medical education, and fostering a learning environment that supports resident growth, scholarly activity, and professional development. This role includes significant collaboration with departmental leadership, medical school administration, affiliated clinical sites, faculty, residents, and institutional Graduate Medical Education (GME) leadership. The mission of the Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine is to advance the health and well-being of our community through educating and training the next generation of physicians - medical students, residents, and fellows - who will thrive as lifelong learners and compassionate, skilled practitioners. Our programs are built on a foundation of evidence-based, patient-centered care and are enriched by a culture of innovation, mentorship, and scholarly growth. Faculty at the Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine benefit from close collaboration across medical specialties and strong partnerships with both community-based and academic healthcare providers, creating a dynamic environment to advance excellence in education, clinical care, and research. We are looking for someone with an innovative spirit and a passion for advancing scientific knowledge and healthcare delivery. This position reports to the department chair with a dotted line to the Designated Institutional Official for GME.  Responsibilities 1. Program Leadership & Administration Oversee all operations of the psychiatry residency program in accordance with ACGME Institutional, Common, and Specialty Requirements. Develop and implement program policies, curricula, evaluation systems, and resident schedules. Lead program accreditation activities, including ACGME Self‑Study, Annual Program Evaluation (APE), and Continuous Quality Improvement (CQI) efforts. In collaboration with the chair, manage program budget and resource allocation to support educational excellence. 2. Curriculum Development & Educational Oversight Design, implement, and continuously refine a competency‑based curriculum that meets all ACGME requirements. Ensure high‑quality clinical, didactic, and simulation‑based education across all training sites. Promote innovative teaching methods and evidence‑based psychiatric practice. 3. Resident Recruitment, Evaluation, and Mentorship Direct the resident recruitment and selection process through ERAS/NRMP. Oversee resident evaluation, Milestones reporting, and semi‑annual performance reviews. Provide individualized mentorship, career guidance, and support for residents. Ensure a safe, supportive learning environment that adheres to ACGME duty‑hour and well‑being standards. 4. Faculty Development & Engagement (in support of the department chair) Recruit, mentor, and evaluate program faculty. Ensure faculty receive ongoing development in teaching, supervision, and evaluation. Promote a culture of professionalism and collaboration. 5. Scholarly Activity & Academic Contribution Foster resident and faculty involvement in research, quality improvement, and scholarly dissemination. Participate in academic productivity, including publications, presentations, or educational innovation. 6. Clinical Excellence Maintain an active clinical practice in psychiatry. Serve as a role model for high‑quality, compassionate, patient‑centered care. Minimum Qualifications: • M.D. or D.O. from an accredited institution and credentials that merit appointment at the rank of associate professor or higher. • Florida medical license or eligibility for licensure, and active or eligible certification by the American Board of Psychiatry and Neurology (ABPN). • Minimum of three years of documented educational and/or administrative experience. • The ability to effectively communicate with students, residents, fellows and employees from various backgrounds is required. Preferred • Prior experience as a program director, associate program director, clerkship director, or other GME leadership role. • Experience with ACGME accreditation, curriculum design, and competency based evaluation. • Record of scholarly activity and participation in academic psychiatry organizations. Salary: Commensurate with Experience College or Department: Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine Location: Clinical - Off Campus Location (COM use only) Work Days and Hours: N/A Application Deadline: 2026-10-16 Special Instructions to Applicant: This recruitment has been reopened; all previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: FAU’s Career Page permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. PLEASE NOTE: A maximum of five (5) documents may be attached to your application. If more than five (5) documents are required for submission, please combine additional documents into a single attachment to not exceed the maximum permitted. The site permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. Candidates wishing full consideration are to provide the following: a cover letter and curriculum vitae. Transcripts: The selected candidate for this position is required to submit an official transcript sent directly from the institution for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Similarly, for degrees from outside the United States, the evaluation by an organization belonging to the National Association of Credential Evaluation (NACES), with an indication of the documents the evaluation was prepared from (official transcripts, diplomas, dissertation abstracts) is required for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Transcripts must be issued to Florida Atlantic University, not to the individual applicant. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Clinical---Off-Campus-Location-COM-use-only/Cardiologist---Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor_REQ21674": {
      "title": "Cardiologist - Assistant/Associate/Full Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU on its race to excellence. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The FAU Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine seeks a dynamic and collaborative Cardiologist to join our clinical faculty at the rank of Assistant/Associate/Full Professor. The successful candidate will be a highly skilled and specialized medical professional responsible for the diagnosis, treatment, and management of a wide range of cardiovascular diseases and conditions. This position offers the opportunity to provide exemplary, compassionate care within the Florida Atlantic Medical Group with a strong emphasis on serving our broad-based patient populations and actively engaging in teaching, mentorship, and scholarly activities within a thriving community-based medical school setting.  The mission of the Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine is to advance the health and well-being of our community through educating and training the next generation of physicians - medical students, residents, and fellows - who will thrive as lifelong learners and compassionate, skilled practitioners. Our programs are built on a foundation of evidence-based, patient-centered care and are enriched by a culture of innovation, mentorship, and scholarly growth. Faculty at the Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine benefit from close collaboration across medical specialties and strong partnerships with both community-based and academic healthcare providers, creating a dynamic environment to advance excellence in education, clinical care, and research. We are looking for someone with an innovative spirit and a passion for advancing scientific knowledge and healthcare delivery. Responsibilities: Clinical Care Provide comprehensive diagnostic and therapeutic care for patients with cardiovascular diseases, including coronary artery disease, heart failure, arrhythmias, valvular disorders, and preventive cardiology, with a focus on improving cardiology health outcomes. Perform invasive and non-invasive cardiac procedures. Collaborate with multidisciplinary teams to ensure safe and coordinated care. Participate in hospital and community-based outreach programs to expand access to cardiovascular healthcare. Research & Scholarship Engage in clinical research, quality improvement, or public health initiatives related to cardiology. Share scholarly efforts through conference presentations and peer-reviewed publications. Service & Community Engagement Serve on departmental, college, and university committees. Collaborate with local agencies and community organizations to improve cardiovascular healthcare delivery and outcomes. Contribute to institutional initiatives aimed at advancing clinical care and community education. Academic Teaching & Mentorship As this is a primarily clinical position, teaching and mentorship are not requirements of the position at this time, however, there may be opportunities to: provide high-quality teaching to medical students, residents, and fellows in clinical and didactic settings. mentor learners in patient care, clinical reasoning, research methodology, and professional development. contribute to curriculum development with emphasis on evidence-based practice and cardiovascular healthcare. Minimum Qualifications: • MD or DO degree from an accredited institution and credentials that merit appointment at the rank of assistant professor or higher required. • A Florida medical license, or the ability to obtain one, and ABMS Board certification or eligibility in Cardiology required. • Demonstrated commitment to academic teaching, scholarship, and community engagement. Preferred Competencies • Evidence of multidisciplinary and interprofessional collaboration. Salary: Commensurate with Experience College or Department: Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine Location: Clinical - Off Campus Location (COM use only) Work Days and Hours: N/A Application Deadline: 2026-10-16 Special Instructions to Applicant: This recruitment has been reopened; all previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: FAU’s Career Page permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. PLEASE NOTE: A maximum of five (5) documents may be attached to your application. If more than five (5) documents are required for submission, please combine additional documents into a single attachment to not exceed the maximum permitted. The site permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. Candidates wishing full consideration are to provide the following: a cover letter and curriculum vitae. Transcripts: The selected candidate for this position is required to submit an official transcript sent directly from the institution for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Similarly, for degrees from outside the United States, the evaluation by an organization belonging to the National Association of Credential Evaluation (NACES), with an indication of the documents the evaluation was prepared from (official transcripts, diplomas, dissertation abstracts) is required for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Transcripts must be issued to Florida Atlantic University, not to the individual applicant. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Clinical---Off-Campus-Location-COM-use-only/Gastroenterologist---Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor_REQ21638": {
      "title": "Gastroenterologist - Assistant/Associate/Full Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU on its race to excellence. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The FAU Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine seeks a dynamic and collaborative Gastroenterologist to join our clinical faculty at the rank of Assistant/Associate/Full Professor. The successful candidate will be a highly skilled physician specializing in the diagnosis, treatment, and management of a wide range of gastrointestinal diseases and conditions. This position offers the opportunity to provide exemplary, compassionate care within the Florida Atlantic Medical Group with a strong emphasis on serving our broad-based patient populations and actively engaging in teaching, mentorship, and scholarly activities within a thriving community-based medical school setting. The mission of the Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine is to advance the health and well-being of our community through educating and training the next generation of physicians - medical students, residents, and fellows - who will thrive as lifelong learners and compassionate, skilled practitioners. Our programs are built on a foundation of evidence-based, patient-centered care and are enriched by a culture of innovation, mentorship, and scholarly growth. Faculty at the Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine benefit from close collaboration across medical specialties and strong partnerships with both community-based and academic healthcare providers, creating a dynamic environment to advance excellence in education, clinical care, and research. We are looking for someone with an innovative spirit and a passion for advancing scientific knowledge and healthcare delivery. Responsibilities: Clinical Care Provide comprehensive diagnostic and therapeutic care for patients with gastrointestinal, hepatic, biliary, and pancreatic disorders, with a focus on improving gastrointestinal health outcomes. Perform diagnostic and therapeutic endoscopic procedures. Collaborate with multidisciplinary teams to ensure safe and coordinated care. Participate in hospital and community-based outreach programs to expand access to gastrointestinal healthcare. Research & Scholarship Engage in clinical research, quality improvement, or public health initiatives related to gastroenterology. Share scholarly efforts through conference presentations and peer-reviewed publications. Service & Community Engagement Serve on departmental, college, and university committees. Collaborate with local agencies and community organizations to improve gastrointestinal healthcare delivery and outcomes. Contribute to institutional initiatives aimed at advancing clinical care and community education. Academic Teaching & Mentorship As this is a primarily clinical position, teaching and mentorship are not requirements of the position at this time, however, there may be future opportunities to: provide high-quality teaching to medical students, residents, and fellows in clinical and didactic settings. mentor learners in patient care, clinical reasoning, research methodology, and professional development. contribute to curriculum development with emphasis on evidence-based practice and gastrointestinal healthcare. Minimum Qualifications: • MD or DO degree from an accredited institution and credentials that merit appointment at the rank of assistant professor or higher required. • A Florida medical license, or the ability to obtain one, and ABMS Board certification or eligibility in Gastroenterology required. • Demonstrated commitment to academic teaching, scholarship, and community engagement. Preferred Competencies • Evidence of multidisciplinary and interprofessional collaboration. Salary: Commensurate with Experience College or Department: Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine Location: Clinical - Off Campus Location (COM use only) Work Days and Hours: N/A Application Deadline: 2026-10-16 Special Instructions to Applicant: This recruitment has been reopened; all previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: FAU’s Career Page permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. PLEASE NOTE: A maximum of five (5) documents may be attached to your application. If more than five (5) documents are required for submission, please combine additional documents into a single attachment to not exceed the maximum permitted. The site permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. Candidates wishing full consideration are to provide the following: a cover letter and curriculum vitae. Transcripts: The selected candidate for this position is required to submit an official transcript sent directly from the institution for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Similarly, for degrees from outside the United States, the evaluation by an organization belonging to the National Association of Credential Evaluation (NACES), with an indication of the documents the evaluation was prepared from (official transcripts, diplomas, dissertation abstracts) is required for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Transcripts must be issued to Florida Atlantic University, not to the individual applicant. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Clinical---Off-Campus-Location-COM-use-only/Orthopedic-Surgeon---Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor_REQ21637": {
      "title": "Orthopedic Surgeon - Assistant/Associate/Full Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU on its race to excellence. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The FAU Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine seeks a dynamic and collaborative Orthopedic Surgeon to join our clinical faculty at the rank of Assistant/Associate/Full Professor. The successful candidate will be a highly skilled and specialized physician responsible for the diagnosis, treatment, and surgical management of musculoskeletal disorders and injuries. This position offers the opportunity to provide exemplary, compassionate care within the Florida Atlantic Medical Group with a strong emphasis on serving our broad-based patient populations and actively engaging in teaching, mentorship, and scholarly activities within a thriving community-based medical school setting. The mission of the Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine is to advance the health and well-being of our community through educating and training the next generation of physicians - medical students, residents, and fellows - who will thrive as lifelong learners and compassionate, skilled practitioners. Our programs are built on a foundation of evidence-based, patient-centered care and are enriched by a culture of innovation, mentorship, and scholarly growth. Faculty at the Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine benefit from close collaboration across medical specialties and strong partnerships with both community-based and academic healthcare providers, creating a dynamic environment to advance excellence in education, clinical care, and research. We are looking for someone with an innovative spirit and a passion for advancing scientific knowledge and healthcare delivery. Responsibilities: Clinical Care Provide comprehensive orthopedic care, including the evaluation and management of musculoskeletal conditions involving bones, joints, ligaments, tendons, and muscles. Perform diagnostic and therapeutic orthopedic surgical procedures. Manage both acute and chronic orthopedic conditions using evidence-based approaches. Collaborate with multidisciplinary teams to ensure safe and coordinated care. Participate in hospital and community-based outreach programs to expand access to orthopedic and musculoskeletal care. Research & Scholarship Engage in clinical research, quality improvement, or public health initiatives related to orthopedic surgery. Share scholarly efforts through conference presentations and peer-reviewed publications. Service & Community Engagement Serve on departmental, college, and university committees. Collaborate with local agencies and community organizations to improve orthopedic healthcare delivery and outcomes. Contribute to institutional initiatives aimed at advancing clinical care and community education. Academic Teaching & Mentorship As this is a primarily clinical position, teaching and mentorship are not requirements of the position at this time, however, there may be future opportunities to: provide high-quality teaching to medical students, residents, and fellows in clinical and didactic settings. mentor learners in patient care, clinical reasoning, research methodology, and professional development. contribute to curriculum development with emphasis on evidence-based practice and orthopedic healthcare. Minimum Qualifications: • MD or DO degree from an accredited institution and credentials that merit appointment at the rank of assistant professor or higher required. • A Florida medical license, or the ability to obtain one, and ABMS Board certification or eligibility in Orthopedic Surgery required. • Demonstrated commitment to academic teaching, scholarship, and community engagement. Preferred Competencies • Evidence of multidisciplinary and interprofessional collaboration. Salary: Commensurate with Experience College or Department: Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine Location: Clinical - Off Campus Location (COM use only) Work Days and Hours: N/A Application Deadline: 2026-10-16 Special Instructions to Applicant: This recruitment has been reopened; all previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: FAU’s Career Page permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. PLEASE NOTE: A maximum of five (5) documents may be attached to your application. If more than five (5) documents are required for submission, please combine additional documents into a single attachment to not exceed the maximum permitted. The site permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. Candidates wishing full consideration are to provide the following: a cover letter and curriculum vitae. Transcripts: The selected candidate for this position is required to submit an official transcript sent directly from the institution for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Similarly, for degrees from outside the United States, the evaluation by an organization belonging to the National Association of Credential Evaluation (NACES), with an indication of the documents the evaluation was prepared from (official transcripts, diplomas, dissertation abstracts) is required for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Transcripts must be issued to Florida Atlantic University, not to the individual applicant. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Clinical---Off-Campus-Location-COM-use-only/Urologist---Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor_REQ21636": {
      "title": "Urologist - Assistant/Associate/Full Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU on its race to excellence. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The FAU Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine seeks a dynamic and collaborative Urologist to join our clinical faculty at the rank of Assistant/Associate/Full Professor. The successful candidate will be a highly skilled and specialized medical professional responsible for the diagnosis, treatment, and management of diseases and conditions of the urinary tract and male reproductive system. This position offers the opportunity to provide exemplary, compassionate care within the Florida Atlantic Medical Group with a strong emphasis on serving our broad-based patient populations and actively engaging in teaching, mentorship, and scholarly activities within a thriving community-based medical school setting. The mission of the Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine is to advance the health and well-being of our community through educating and training the next generation of physicians - medical students, residents, and fellows - who will thrive as lifelong learners and compassionate, skilled practitioners. Our programs are built on a foundation of evidence-based, patient-centered care and are enriched by a culture of innovation, mentorship, and scholarly growth. Faculty at the Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine benefit from close collaboration across medical specialties and strong partnerships with both community-based and academic healthcare providers, creating a dynamic environment to advance excellence in education, clinical care, and research. We are looking for someone with an innovative spirit and a passion for advancing scientific knowledge and healthcare delivery. Responsibilities: Clinical Care Provide comprehensive diagnostic, medical, and surgical management for patients with urologic conditions including kidney, bladder, prostate, adrenal, and male reproductive disorders, with a focus on improving urological health outcomes. Perform diagnostic and therapeutic urologic procedures. Collaborate with multidisciplinary teams to ensure safe and coordinated care. Participate in hospital and community-based outreach programs to expand access to urological healthcare. Research & Scholarship Engage in clinical research, quality improvement, or public health initiatives related to urology. Share scholarly efforts through conference presentations and peer-reviewed publications. Service & Community Engagement Serve on departmental, college, and university committees. Collaborate with local agencies and community organizations to improve urological healthcare delivery and outcomes. Contribute to institutional initiatives aimed at advancing clinical care and community education. Academic Teaching & Mentorship As this is a primarily clinical position, teaching and mentorship are not requirements of the position at this time, however, there may be future opportunities to: provide high-quality teaching to medical students, residents, and fellows in clinical and didactic settings. mentor learners in patient care, clinical reasoning, research methodology, and professional development. contribute to curriculum development with emphasis on evidence-based practice and urological healthcare. Minimum Qualifications: • MD or DO degree from an accredited institution and credentials that merit appointment at the rank of assistant professor or higher required. • A Florida medical license, or the ability to obtain one, and ABMS Board certification or eligibility in Urology required. • Demonstrated commitment to academic teaching, scholarship, and community engagement. Preferred Competencies • Evidence of multidisciplinary and interprofessional collaboration. Salary: Commensurate with Experience College or Department: Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine Location: Clinical - Off Campus Location (COM use only) Work Days and Hours: N/A Application Deadline: 2026-10-16 Special Instructions to Applicant: This recruitment has been reopened; all previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: FAU’s Career Page permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. PLEASE NOTE: A maximum of five (5) documents may be attached to your application. If more than five (5) documents are required for submission, please combine additional documents into a single attachment to not exceed the maximum permitted. The site permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. Candidates wishing full consideration are to provide the following: a cover letter and curriculum vitae. Transcripts: The selected candidate for this position is required to submit an official transcript sent directly from the institution for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Similarly, for degrees from outside the United States, the evaluation by an organization belonging to the National Association of Credential Evaluation (NACES), with an indication of the documents the evaluation was prepared from (official transcripts, diplomas, dissertation abstracts) is required for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Transcripts must be issued to Florida Atlantic University, not to the individual applicant. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Nursing-Adjuncts_REQ21767": {
      "title": "Nursing Adjuncts",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nApply now to join FAU on its race to excellence. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The College of Nursing (CON) seeks qualified Nursing Adjuncts to support the teaching mission of the college by providing high-quality instruction in classroom, laboratory, simulation, and/or clinical settings. Adjuncts are part-time instructional professionals who bring current clinical expertise to the learning environment and support the preparation of future nurses through teaching, mentoring, and evaluation of students. Adjuncts will contribute to the college’s caring-based educational philosophy by fostering a supportive and engaging learning environment for students. Responsibilities may include teaching undergraduate nursing courses, supervising clinical practice experiences, evaluating student performance, maintaining course materials in the learning management system, and collaborating with course coordinators and program leadership to ensure course objectives and accreditation standards are met. The College of Nursing is known for its commitment to caring science and preparing nurses who are competent, compassionate, and responsive to the health needs of various communities. Adjuncts support this mission by bringing real-world clinical practice into the academic setting and helping students integrate theory with professional nursing practice. Minimum Qualifications: o Baccalaureate degree in nursing (BSN) from an accredited institution, five years of experience in nursing, and certification in clinical area of teaching; or Master’s degree in Nursing (MSN) from an accredited institution o Current, unencumbered Registered Nurse (RN) license o Minimum of two years of professional nursing practice experience in the specialty area relevant to the teaching assignment Salary: Commensurate with Experience College or Department: Christine E. Lynn College of Nursing Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: N/A Application Deadline: 2027-01-30 Special Instructions to Applicant: This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: FAU’s Career Page permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. PLEASE NOTE: A maximum of five (5) documents may be attached to your application. If more than five (5) documents are required for submission, please combine additional documents into a single attachment to not exceed the maximum permitted. The site permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. Candidates wishing full consideration are to provide the following: o CV o Copy of current RN licensure o Official transcript o 2 letters of reference o Copy of current malpractice insurance coverage o Copy of current CPR certification Transcripts: The selected candidate for this position is required to submit an official transcript sent directly from the institution for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Similarly, for degrees from outside the United States, the evaluation by an organization belonging to the National Association of Credential Evaluation (NACES), with an indication of the documents the evaluation was prepared from (official transcripts, diplomas, dissertation abstracts) is required for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Transcripts must be issued to Florida Atlantic University, not to the individual applicant. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Harbor-Branch-HBOI/Postdoctoral-Fellow-Application-of-Machine-Learning-and-Robotics_REQ21771": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow Application of Machine Learning and Robotics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-25\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU on its race to excellence. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University's Systems and Imaging Laboratory (SAIL) at Harbor Branch Oceanographic Institute in Fort Pierce, FL, is seeking a 12-month, non-tenure Postdoctoral Fellow position. Extension of the appointment beyond one year is possible, depending on funding availability and performance. This position will focus on developing robotics and cyber physical systems solutions using machine learning and artificial intelligence to support different aspects of marine science, with opportunities to expand to other areas. Currently, SAIL is conducting multiple projects ranging from Hybrid Aerial Underwater Robotic System (HAUCS)– a cyber physical system (CPS) for aquaculture, to sensors and platforms for maritime applications. In this position, your primary task will be to lead the development of algorithms, software, and hardware to extend the current HAUCS framework. This includes developing the sensors, sensing robotic platforms, environmental prediction models, and visualization tools as needed. Additional tasks include field experiments to test the instruments and validate models; preparing data reports and presentations for technical conferences; publishing results in peer-reviewed journals; and mentoring students and junior scientists. There will also be opportunities to work on other related projects, including the application of AI to solve underwater vision problems and Phase III of the Next Generation Sensor Systems for Natural Oceanic Bioluminescence Assessments. The Postdoctoral Fellow will be able to grow his/her skills in research and grant writing by taking an active role in identifying funding opportunities and developing grant proposals. Minimum Qualifications: - A doctorate (foreign equivalent acceptable) in electrical engineering, computer science, engineering, or related area. - A team player who is willing to train junior scientists in the lab. - Expertise in robotics and unmanned aerial vehicle development, in particular electronic hardware design and embedded system development. - Comprehension of common machine learning algorithms and image analysis. - Independent, self-motivated, well-organized, and critical thinker. - Good written and verbal communication skills. Salary: $55,000.00 - $65,000.00 College or Department: Harbor Branch Oceanographic Institute/Systems and Imaging Lab (SAIL) Location: Harbor Branch (HBOI) Work Days and Hours: N/A Application Deadline: 2026-12-31 Special Instructions to Applicant: This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: FAU’s Career Page permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. PLEASE NOTE: A maximum of five (5) documents may be attached to your application. If more than five (5) documents are required for submission, please combine additional documents into a single attachment to not exceed the maximum permitted. The site permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. Candidates wishing full consideration are to provide the following: a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of interest, transcripts, and contact information for three professional references including email addresses and phone numbers. Transcripts: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Assistant-Professor-of-Teaching_REQ22102": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Teaching",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU on its race to excellence. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The Department of Civil, Environmental & Geomatics Engineering ( http://www.cege.fau.edu/ ) at Florida Atlantic University welcomes applications for a non-tenure-track Assistant Teaching Professor position in Civil, Environmental and Geomatics Engineering. The department is particularly interested in a candidate who holds a Professional Engineer (P.E.) license and whose expertise in civil and environmental engineering includes significant design experience in the preparation of plans, specifications, and engineering studies. Candidates whose academic work focuses on applied, industry-relevant transportation problems or emerging analytical methods in the field are strongly encouraged to apply. The position is expected to teach structural analysis, drawings classes, and design-related classes including senior design capstone. The Department of Civil, Environmental & Geomatics Engineering ( CEGE ) hosts 3 ABET-accredited undergraduate programs, a Master’s degree in Civil Engineering, and a Ph.D. in Transportation and Environmental Engineering with about 400 undergraduate and 100 graduate students. The faculty is highly interdisciplinary and conducts research primarily in the broad thematic areas of Urban Mobility, Infrastructure, and Sustainability/Resilience. The Department has three research centers: the Center for Infrastructure and Constructed Facilities ( fau.edu/engineering/cege/research/cicf/ ), the Center for Water Resiliency and Risk Reduction ( cwr3.fau.edu ), and the Freight Mobility Research Institute ( fmri.fau.edu ).   The FAU College of Engineering and Computer Science is in the top three fastest progressing engineering colleges in the nation (US News and World Report Rankings 2020-2022). The college offers degrees with a modern twist that bear specializations in areas of national priority such as artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, internet-of-things, transportation and supply chain management, and data science. For more information about the college, please visit eng.fau.edu . Florida Atlantic University, established in 1961, officially opened its doors in 1964 as the fifth public university in Florida. Today, the university serves more than 31,000 undergraduate and graduate students across six campuses located along the southeast Florida coast. In recent years, the university has doubled its research expenditure and outpaced its peers in student achievement rates. FAU is ranked as a top 100 public university by U.S. News & World Report. In 2025, the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education designated Florida Atlantic as R1: Very High Research Spending and Doctorate Production – the most prestigious research accolade in the country. For more information about FAU, visit  www.fau.edu . Appointments are expected to start in Fall 2026. Minimum Qualifications: • Applicants must have a B.S. degree and a Ph.D. in civil or environmental engineering or a closely related engineering discipline, with a Professional Engineer (P.E.) license in the State of Florida, or in another state with the ability to acquire such a license in Florida. • Demonstrated ability in communication, interpersonal skills, collaboration, leadership, and student motivation are required attributes. • Expected to teach and mentor graduate and undergraduate students and to participate in professional and departmental service activities. • Candidates are expected to become familiar with new pedagogies such as active learning and AI literacy in civil and environmental engineering, including re-creating knowledge for educating and nurturing students and translating knowledge into practice. Salary: Commensurate with Experience College or Department: College of Engineering and Computer Science Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: N/A Application Deadline: 2026-12-31 Special Instructions to Applicant: This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: FAU’s Career Page permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. PLEASE NOTE: A maximum of five (5) documents may be attached to your application. If more than five (5) documents are required for submission, please combine additional documents into a single attachment to not exceed the maximum permitted. The site permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. Candidates wishing full consideration are to provide the following in PDF format: a letter of interest that incorporates research and teaching statements, an up-to-date CV, and names of three references. Transcripts: The selected candidate for this position is required to submit an official transcript sent directly from the institution for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Similarly, for degrees from outside the United States, the evaluation by an organization belonging to the National Association of Credential Evaluation (NACES), with an indication of the documents the evaluation was prepared from (official transcripts, diplomas, dissertation abstracts) is required for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Transcripts must be issued to Florida Atlantic University, not to the individual applicant. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Graduate-Nursing-Adjuncts_REQ21774": {
      "title": "Graduate Nursing Adjuncts",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-03-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nApply now to join FAU on its race to excellence. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The Christine E. Lynn College of Nursing at Florida Atlantic University invites applications for Graduate Nursing Adjuncts to support the Master of Science in Nursing (MSN), and Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP). Adjuncts are part-time instructional professionals who contribute specialized expertise in advanced nursing practice and support the academic preparation of graduate nursing students. Graduate adjuncts may teach didactic, clinical, laboratory, or online courses and collaborate with course coordinators and program leadership to ensure alignment with program outcomes, accreditation standards, and evidence-based nursing practice. Responsibilities include facilitating student learning, evaluating student performance, maintaining course materials within the university’s learning management system, and providing guidance and mentorship to graduate nursing students. Adjuncts are expected to support the College’s caring-based philosophy and integrate clinical expertise, scholarship, and professional experience into the educational environment. The College is internationally recognized for its commitment to caring science—expanding the science of caring, practicing the art of nursing, studying its meaning, and living it in academic and clinical practice. Adjunct appointments are part-time and assigned per course, per semester, based on program needs and enrollment. Typical Responsibilities Supervise and evaluate graduate nursing students in advanced practice clinical settings Teach graduate nursing courses in classroom, online, simulation, or clinical environments Collaborate with course coordinators and faculty to ensure consistency in course delivery and student learning outcomes  Evaluate student assignments, clinical performance, and competencies  Maintain accurate course records, grades, and student evaluations  Participate in adjunct orientation and comply with university and college policies  Provide mentorship and professional guidance to students preparing for advanced nursing roles Minimum Qualifications: o MSN degree/post-graduate certificate in an area of advanced practice specialty and three years of experience working as an advanced practice nurse in area of specialty (Clinical adjunct positions only) o National certification as an Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN) or specialty certification where appropriate o Current, unencumbered Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN) or Registered Nurse (RN) license in Florida (or eligibility for licensure) Salary: Commensurate with Experience College or Department: Christine E. Lynn College of Nursing Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: N/A Application Deadline: 2026-12-31 Special Instructions to Applicant: This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: FAU’s Career Page permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. PLEASE NOTE: A maximum of five (5) documents may be attached to your application. If more than five (5) documents are required for submission, please combine additional documents into a single attachment to not exceed the maximum permitted. The site permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. Candidates wishing full consideration are to provide the following: o CV o Copy of current RN licensure o Official transcript from master's program (doctoral program, if applicable) o 2 letters of reference o Copy of current malpractice insurance coverage o Copy of current CPR certification Transcripts: The selected candidate for this position is required to submit an official transcript sent directly from the institution for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Similarly, for degrees from outside the United States, the evaluation by an organization belonging to the National Association of Credential Evaluation (NACES), with an indication of the documents the evaluation was prepared from (official transcripts, diplomas, dissertation abstracts) is required for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Transcripts must be issued to Florida Atlantic University, not to the individual applicant. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    }
  },
